WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.120
On an ordinary day in 1991, a young man known
by the initials J.S. went on a hike with four

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:08.880
of his friends on the wooded outskirts of
their small town.

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:14.520
Everything seemed perfectly normal until J.S.
began to feel a strange sense of familiarity,

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:16.740
like he had been in this spot before.

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:20.160
He couldn’t shake this weird feeling, but
thought nothing more of it.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:23.880
Little did he know that this was a sign of
deadly things to come.

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:29.280
Several hours after first experiencing that
sense of deja vu, J.S. was found by the side

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:33.780
of the road, covered in cuts and scratches,
with his friends nowhere to be found.

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:40.260
This is the story of SCP - 939, an unforgettable
monster that you’ll never remember.

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:45.480
There was no way for J.S. to know that the
unsettling feeling he felt and the horrors

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:51.060
that followed it were the result of an experiment
conducted by the SCP Foundation, an experiment

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:53.100
with deadly unforeseen consequences.

00:00:53.940 --> 00:01:00.000
J.S. and his friends were exposed to a substance
known only as AMN-C227 as part of a series

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.460
of tests performed by the SCP Foundation intended
to determine the effectiveness of this substance

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:07.260
as a deliberate amnestic.

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:14.400
Dealing with as many mysterious, secret creatures
and objects as they do, the SCP Foundation

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:19.260
has long needed a way to tamper with the memories
of those exposed to the foundation’s various

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:24.840
prisoners and test subjects, and, when the
foundation discovered AMN-C227, it seemed

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:26.760
like it might be perfect for this purpose.

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:30.240
So where did AMN-C227 come from?

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:35.520
Over a year before the incident with J.S.
and his friends, the SCP Foundation captured

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:37.020
SCP-939.

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:42.780
SCP-939 is a species of endothermic predators
that live and hunt in packs.

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:48.180
They are designated Keter class, and regarded
as highly dangerous and hostile to human life.

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:55.080
Native to caves, they have no eyes, translucent
red skin, and stand at an average of 2.2 meters

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:58.020
tall, with an average weight of 250 kg.

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:01.800
They have four limbs, each&nbsp;
ending in three-fingered&nbsp;

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:04.260
claws and a fourth opposable digit resembling

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:04.680
a thumb.

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:09.900
In addition to their sharp claws, their mouths
are filled with red, fang-like teeth that

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:12.300
reach up to 6 cm in length.

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:15.120
In place of their absent eyes,&nbsp;
they have light-sensitive&nbsp;

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:18.120
spots running along their backs, which are

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:22.140
covered in spines believed to detect changes
in air pressure and flow.

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:27.660
In addition to their many other terrifying
attributes, the internal anatomy of SCP-939

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:29.640
poses a biological mystery.

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:33.420
These creatures have no circulatory system
and no digestive tract.

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:38.760
That’s right, in spite of being predators
seemingly acting on a need to feed, they have

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:39.360
no stomach.

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:44.160
Instead, when they eat their food builds up
in their respiratory system until its presence

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:47.280
inhibits function, and then it is regurgitated.

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:52.260
In spite of being a creature that should not,
under any logical conditions, be able to live,

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:58.740
SCP-939 continues to persist, and is even
capable of giving birth to live young after

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:00.900
a gestation period of 12 months.

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:05.880
The SCP Foundation was able to study a litter
of these young that were born in captivity

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:11.040
in September of 1992, though the creatures
remain just as much of a scientific mystery

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:12.900
as they were upon first discovery.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:18.540
Everything about them seems to defy the logic
of the natural world - which, to be fair,

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:20.520
is really nothing new for the Foundation.

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:27.180
The respiratory system of SCP-939 was found
to exhale small traces of an airborne amnestic

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:30.540
substance, given the name AMN-C227.

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:35.460
This compound blocks the formation of memories
for the duration of exposure to it, plus a

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:38.640
thirty minute period following the exposure,
give or take a few minutes.

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:44.160
It is colorless, odorless, tasteless, and
completely undetectable in the bloodstream

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:45.900
after only 60 minutes.

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:52.560
AMN-C227 was approved for use as a Class C
Amnestic by the SCP Foundation in 1990 following

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:53.640
some initial tests.

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:58.800
However, after one particular incident involving
a young man and his friends, the official

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:01.320
use of AMN-C227 was suspended.

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:07.500
J.S. and three of his four friends were previously
given a dose of AMN-C227, though the details

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:10.560
of why they were given the amnestic have since
been stricken from the record.

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:17.160
Several months after being exposed to AMN-C227,
J.S. and friends went out on their ill-fated

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:17.880
hiking trip.

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:21.720
While hiking, J.S. was suddenly overcome with
a sense of deja vu.

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:25.140
When he mentioned it to his friends, three
of them agreed that they felt it too.

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:27.360
One of the group, another young man - who&nbsp;

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:30.540
had not been exposed to&nbsp;
AMN-C227 - was uncomfortable

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:31.800
and decided to go home.

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:36.600
J.S. and the remaining three members of the
group made the choice to stay in the woods

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:40.560
and try to determine what was triggering the
unusual feeling of familiarity.

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:45.660
As they got closer and closer to a large cave
near the hiking trail, the sense of having

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:48.360
been there before grew stronger and stronger.

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:54.180
Armed with only one flashlight and a foolish
curiosity, the four went inside the cave.

00:04:54.720 --> 00:05:00.720
They made their way deeper and deeper into
the darkness, not knowing why they felt this

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:02.400
way or what they might find inside.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:07.440
None of the group could explain just what
felt so familiar, only that the further they

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:11.100
made their way into the cave, the more pronounced
the feeling became.

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:15.240
It was getting late, and they knew they should
have been afraid to venture so deep into a

00:05:15.240 --> 00:05:20.760
cave with only one light source and no knowledge
of what lay inside, but still they pressed

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:20.940
on.

00:05:20.940 --> 00:05:24.840
One of the group remarked that they should
turn back, but the others refused to listen.

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:28.860
They wanted to know what they were getting
close to, what was drawing them deeper and

00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:29.880
deeper into the cave.

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:33.120
Unfortunately for them, they would get their
answer.

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:39.120
In the heart of the cave was a pack of SCP-939,
waiting patiently for their prey to wander

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:39.960
into their domain.

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:43.920
There are no witnesses to account for what
exactly happened to J.S. and his companions,

00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:47.580
but we can reasonably piece the events together
from what happened after.

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:51.780
Once the friends reached the heart of the
cave, the creatures were on them in seconds,

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:55.140
raking them with their sharp claws and biting
with their fangs.

00:05:55.140 --> 00:06:00.480
SCP-939 are larger and stronger than most
people, so it was probably not much of a fight.

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:05.280
However, while his friends were being devoured,
J.S. was somehow able to scramble out of the

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:07.860
cave and make his way into the woods in search
of help.

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:12.600
Under the influence of the AMN-C227 that had
built up in the cave from the presence of

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:17.640
the pack of SCP-939, J.S. lost a large portion
of his memory of the event.

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:22.500
He found himself on the side of the highway
late at night, seriously injured and his clothes

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:23.100
ripped.

00:06:23.100 --> 00:06:27.600
An officer found him there, and asked him
to stay still and remain calm until an ambulance

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:28.140
could arrive.

00:06:28.140 --> 00:06:33.180
J.S. was still in a panic and attempted to
run away from the officer, begging to be released

00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:34.080
so that he could get away.

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:39.180
He babbled incoherently about the color red,
screaming over and over again about the “red,”

00:06:39.180 --> 00:06:43.200
though when prompted he could not explain
what the “red” he was screaming about

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:44.100
referred to.

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:45.660
His friends were not with him.

00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:49.740
Just as the officer managed to calm J.S.,
the ambulance arrived.

00:06:49.740 --> 00:06:54.600
Its flashing red lights sent him into another
frenzy, and he attempted to escape custody,

00:06:54.600 --> 00:06:57.060
claiming that the red lights were “going
to get” him.

00:06:57.060 --> 00:07:01.440
The official police report described J.S.
as perhaps being under the influence of a

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:02.460
powerful hallucinogen.

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:06.780
That he was just having a “bad trip,”
but the SCP foundation knew better.

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:12.000
The foundation conducted an interview with
J.S. about his experience, and determined

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:15.060
that SCP-939 was certainly involved.

00:07:15.060 --> 00:07:19.680
As part of their cover-up effort, they strongly
implicated J.S. in the disappearance and death

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:20.220
of his friends.

00:07:20.220 --> 00:07:24.240
He was convicted of manslaughter, though the
bodies of his friends were never found.

00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:29.640
It is rumored that the SCP Foundation hired
him on a prison work release program, and

00:07:29.640 --> 00:07:33.900
that he now works as a member of the janitorial
staff at one of the Foundation’s facilities.

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:40.200
This incident led to the suspension of the
use of AMN-C227, as it revealed some vital

00:07:40.200 --> 00:07:43.080
and disturbing information about the compound’s
side effects.

00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:48.840
After exposure to AMN-C227, a person who found
themselves exposed to it again would experience

00:07:48.840 --> 00:07:53.220
a sense of familiarity, and feel compelled
to investigate the source of this feeling.

00:07:53.220 --> 00:07:59.400
Essentially, anyone treated with AMN-C227
and not made aware of the existence - and

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:05.160
danger - of SCP-939 would become a perfect
victim, primed to be attracted to dens of

00:08:05.160 --> 00:08:06.600
SCP-939.

00:08:06.600 --> 00:08:11.460
It is likely that this side effect is not
a coincidence, but rather a deliberate hunting

00:08:11.460 --> 00:08:15.060
tactic designed to attract prey that had somehow
managed to escape.

00:08:15.060 --> 00:08:21.000
With no memory of their attack at the hands
of SCP-939, this previous intended prey would

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:25.680
find themselves drawn to the same den or even
a new one, not knowing that they were walking

00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:27.600
back into near certain death.

00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:33.600
While the SCP foundation suspended the use
of AMN-C227 as a Class C amnestic, they did

00:08:33.600 --> 00:08:37.680
recruit a team of SCP field operatives to
take advantage of this side effect.

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:40.440
This team of operatives was&nbsp;
deliberately administered&nbsp;

00:08:40.440 --> 00:08:43.800
a dose of AMN-C227 and briefed on its effects,

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:48.120
as well as the dangers of following the feeling
of deja vu should it surface in the field.

00:08:48.120 --> 00:08:53.640
These infected officers were essentially used
as bloodhounds, relying on any sense of unusual

00:08:53.640 --> 00:08:59.640
familiarity to sniff out new dens of SCP-939
so that they could be captured and contained

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:00.420
by the foundation.

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:04.740
As far as we know, this operation is still
ongoing today.

00:09:04.740 --> 00:09:10.260
However, now that the foundation has a sufficient
number of specimens to study, additional dens

00:09:10.260 --> 00:09:14.460
of SCP-939 that are discovered are ordered
to be immediately destroyed.

00:09:14.460 --> 00:09:17.100
As for the SCP-939 still in captivity?

00:09:17.100 --> 00:09:21.900
They are contained in environmentally regulated
and negatively pressurized cells with walls

00:09:21.900 --> 00:09:23.040
of reinforced concrete.

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:29.220
The doors to the cells are air-tight to prevent
the leakage of any AMN-C227, and any personnel

00:09:29.220 --> 00:09:33.600
that interact with one of the creatures is
required to wear Level C Hazmat gear to avoid

00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:37.740
exposure, and follow decontamination procedures
upon exiting the cell.

00:09:37.740 --> 00:09:43.680
All SCP-939 have subdermal tracking devices
implanted to find them in the event of escape.

00:09:44.400 --> 00:09:49.524
Only one SCP-939 has given birth in the time
that the creatures have been in captivity,

00:09:49.524 --> 00:09:49.560
and only one of the litter survived.

00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:55.920
Strangely, SCP-939 young look indistinguishable
from human infants, and change their physical

00:09:55.920 --> 00:09:58.680
appearance at some yet unknown point as they
age.

00:09:58.680 --> 00:10:03.600
If any more offspring are produced, they will
immediately be separated from the parent and

00:10:03.600 --> 00:10:03.960
studied.

00:10:03.960 --> 00:10:04.192
The SCP foundation has redacted all information
about the location of these creatures or the

00:10:04.192 --> 00:10:04.380
incident involving J.S., refusing to reveal
where their natural habitat is.

00:10:04.380 --> 00:10:08.880
All that we know is that they are found in
caves in the woods outside of a small town.

00:10:08.880 --> 00:10:12.000
It could be any town, even yours.

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:16.980
Sp if you’re ever out hiking, and are struck
with a sudden feeling of deja vu?

00:10:17.640 --> 00:10:21.960
Don’t investigate, don’t get curious,
just go home.

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:24.420
It might just save your life.

00:10:24.420 --> 00:10:30.660
The fabric of our world is littered with doorways&nbsp;
if you know where to look for them. Tears,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.660 --> 00:10:38.100
portals, anomalies, all leading to places and&nbsp;
planes beyond human imagining and understanding,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.100 --> 00:10:44.880
and SCP-2317, otherwise known as A Door to&nbsp;
Another World, certainly fits that description.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.540 --> 00:10:51.780
Contained and kept at all times under the watch&nbsp;
of armed guards, SCP-2317 appears to be a simple&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.780 --> 00:10:57.000
and unsuspecting wooden door in its frame.&nbsp;
It hardly looks like it requires such extreme&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.000 --> 00:11:02.340
round-the-clock security or needs a strange,&nbsp;
secretive ritual that the Foundation performs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.340 --> 00:11:08.460
presumably to keep the door closed. But, of&nbsp;
course, sometimes the most interesting thing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:08.460 --> 00:11:12.900
about a closed doorway isn’t where&nbsp;
it leads, it’s what it keeps out.&nbsp;

00:11:13.920 --> 00:11:19.620
Even by the Foundation’s already-high standards,&nbsp;
the requirements and regulations for personnel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.620 --> 00:11:26.580
who are assigned to SCP-2317 seem oddly specific.&nbsp;
Psychological testing is standard practice for to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:31.200
work for the Foundation, but an additional&nbsp;
hurdle that anyone has to clear before even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.200 --> 00:11:36.000
getting to glimpse at this unassuming wooden&nbsp;
door is having a score of at least seventy-two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:42.060
on the Milgram Obedience Examination. It is also&nbsp;
mandatory that personnel assigned to maintaining&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.060 --> 00:11:47.220
it are both unmarried, with no children&nbsp;
or next-of-kin, as well as an unwavering,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:52.980
unquestioning loyalty to the Foundation,&nbsp;
pure devotion to its code and objectives.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:53.760 --> 00:12:00.840
These may seem like strange requirements,&nbsp;
after all, SCP-2317 is just a door…isn’t it?&nbsp;

00:12:01.860 --> 00:12:07.140
Perhaps there’s a reason that the Foundation&nbsp;
keeps so much of the information about SCP-2317&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.140 --> 00:12:13.020
buried deep under layers upon layers of security,&nbsp;
with only the Overseer Council privy to the full&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:13.020 --> 00:12:20.400
details of its strange nature. Knowledge, as they&nbsp;
say, is power - but maybe knowing too much about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:20.400 --> 00:12:27.660
whatever is behind that door can prove deadly.&nbsp;
Still, if SCP-2317 is a Door to Another World,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:27.660 --> 00:12:33.600
an alternate dimension or parallel reality,&nbsp;
it must be safe enough to visit. After all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:33.600 --> 00:12:38.460
the Foundation has been sending personnel&nbsp;
in there on a regular basis. Daily, in fact.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:39.420 --> 00:12:43.500
According to the O5 Council, this&nbsp;
is done as part of a procedure to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:43.500 --> 00:12:49.440
maintain Active Containment of…something&nbsp;
lurking beyond that old wooden doorframe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:50.100 --> 00:12:53.520
But what could possibly warrant such&nbsp;
constant maintenance and surveillance?&nbsp;

00:12:55.140 --> 00:12:59.940
In accordance with the Foundation’s guidelines,&nbsp;
all staff are required to rotate out of observing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:59.940 --> 00:13:05.880
SCP-2317 after every two months and spend the&nbsp;
following third month in full psychological&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:05.880 --> 00:13:10.740
counselling before they are permitted to return to&nbsp;
the containment unit housing the Door to Another&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:10.740 --> 00:13:16.080
World. It was after one of these month-long&nbsp;
periods of evaluation that a Foundation guard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:16.080 --> 00:13:20.640
was informed that his security clearance&nbsp;
had been raised to Level 3 and that he’d&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:20.640 --> 00:13:25.740
been selected for the duty of carrying out&nbsp;
220-Calabasas. He knew the name instantly;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:25.740 --> 00:13:31.500
this was the title given to the daily containment&nbsp;
procedure that absolutely had to be carried out.&nbsp;

00:13:32.460 --> 00:13:36.900
The guard didn’t question these orders, after&nbsp;
all, he’d been selected precisely because of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:36.900 --> 00:13:42.540
his loyalty to the Foundation. He did make one&nbsp;
request to his commanding officer, however:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:42.540 --> 00:13:46.320
he wanted to know what had happened to the&nbsp;
last guard that had performed the procedure.&nbsp;

00:13:47.220 --> 00:13:51.360
“Didn’t make it out of psychological&nbsp;
evaluation,” the officer replied.&nbsp;

00:13:52.320 --> 00:13:57.720
Not letting this affect his dedication, the guard&nbsp;
was told to prepare for Procedure 220-Calabasas.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:58.380 --> 00:14:03.420
Along with a fellow member of Foundation security&nbsp;
personnel, the guard was instructed to gather&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:03.420 --> 00:14:08.880
everything on a strange list. The first was&nbsp;
a pre-selected member of Class-D Personnel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:09.420 --> 00:14:14.460
specifically a convicted murderer. Class-D&nbsp;
refers to ‘Disposable Class’ personnel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:14.460 --> 00:14:20.100
expendable individuals recruited by the&nbsp;
Foundation for the sole purpose of testing SCPs.&nbsp;

00:14:21.180 --> 00:14:26.280
Class-Ds were usually prison inmates&nbsp;
repurposed for SCP testing, and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:26.280 --> 00:14:31.860
one chosen for 220-Calabasas was no exception,&nbsp;
serving multiple life sentences for murders,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:31.860 --> 00:14:35.700
or at least that was what the guard&nbsp;
had been told. A Foundation personnel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:35.700 --> 00:14:40.020
member instructed him to refer to the Class-D&nbsp;
solely as the ‘assistant’ from that point on.&nbsp;

00:14:40.800 --> 00:14:44.700
Next, the guard collected a live&nbsp;
chicken, an obsidian-edged knife,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:44.700 --> 00:14:50.700
a silver aspergillum and aspersorium, to be&nbsp;
filled with 500ccs of Holy Water that had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:50.700 --> 00:14:57.000
been blessed by a priest of the Abrahamic faith,&nbsp;
and finally a one-kiloton nuclear device, which,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:57.000 --> 00:15:01.200
according to instructions, was to only&nbsp;
be detonated in the unlikely event of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:01.200 --> 00:15:04.980
catastrophic containment failure.&nbsp;
In other words, the last resort.&nbsp;

00:15:06.540 --> 00:15:11.700
After following his instructions to the letter and&nbsp;
without question, the guard and his colleague were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:11.700 --> 00:15:16.320
briefed. The Foundation personnel member informed&nbsp;
them that he’d be joining and leading them in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:16.320 --> 00:15:21.480
procedure. The staff member also specified that&nbsp;
henceforth he be referred to as the ‘celebrant’&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:21.480 --> 00:15:27.180
until the completion of 220-Calabasas. The&nbsp;
guard was acutely aware of how specific these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:27.180 --> 00:15:32.220
instructions were, but trusted in the Foundation,&nbsp;
knowing that if they wanted this procedure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:32.220 --> 00:15:36.960
performed a certain way, then it was in everyones’&nbsp;
best interest to carry out the orders to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:36.960 --> 00:15:43.860
letter. But what the celebrant then went on to&nbsp;
explain, raised far more questions about SCP-2317&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:43.860 --> 00:15:51.960
and the nature of Procedure 220-Calabasas. The&nbsp;
Class-D joining them, wasn’t actually a Class-D.&nbsp;

00:15:52.680 --> 00:15:57.420
The assistant, as they were now referred to,&nbsp;
was in reality another Foundation staff member,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:57.420 --> 00:16:02.760
with a Level 4 security clearance,&nbsp;
specifically tailored to SCP-2317.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:03.600 --> 00:16:10.380
Every member of staff entering through SCP-2317&nbsp;
and taking an active role in 220-Calabasas needed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:10.380 --> 00:16:15.060
to be informed that this assistant was not to be&nbsp;
harmed or treated as a member of Disposable Class.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:15.960 --> 00:16:20.880
Fighting back the nagging question of why&nbsp;
the Foundation would employ this subterfuge,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:20.880 --> 00:16:25.140
the guard, along with his fellow security&nbsp;
officer, the celebrant and assistant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:25.140 --> 00:16:29.280
prepared for their departure through&nbsp;
the Door to Another World at solar noon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:29.280 --> 00:16:36.540
when the sun was highest over SCP-2317.&nbsp;
Solar noon, chickens and holy water,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:37.380 --> 00:16:40.860
this all seemed like an oddly-occult&nbsp;
combination for the Foundation.&nbsp;

00:16:41.820 --> 00:16:46.560
As they entered the old wooden door, beyond&nbsp;
lay a barren salt plane, stretching out for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:46.560 --> 00:16:51.900
kilometers in every direction. This alternate&nbsp;
dimension, according to the briefing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:51.900 --> 00:16:58.140
was designated SCP-2317-Prime. The guard&nbsp;
immediately noticed a ring of seven pillars&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:58.140 --> 00:17:03.240
directly ahead of the group as they entered, each&nbsp;
of them bearing intricately-detailed engravings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:03.240 --> 00:17:09.960
unlike anything from any era of ancient history.
Procedure 220-Calabasas was carried out quickly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:09.960 --> 00:17:15.300
but carefully, the guard watching as the celebrant&nbsp;
and assistant were careful not to miss a step.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:16.260 --> 00:17:19.920
First, the celebrant scattered Holy Water&nbsp;
into the center of the pillars with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:19.920 --> 00:17:25.080
aspergillum and aspersorium, looking down&nbsp;
at his feet and keeping a steady pace as he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:25.080 --> 00:17:30.240
stepped counter-clockwise around them. The guard&nbsp;
watched intently as the celebrant completed his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:30.240 --> 00:17:35.340
circuit around the pillars and turned to the&nbsp;
assistant, anointing his head with Holy Water.&nbsp;

00:17:36.060 --> 00:17:42.960
“Seven Seals, Seven Rings, Seven Thrones&nbsp;
for the Scarlet King,” he said aloud.&nbsp;

00:17:43.740 --> 00:17:47.880
The assistant, with the obsidian blade in&nbsp;
his hand, took the chicken and dispatched it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:47.880 --> 00:17:53.640
in sacrifice, letting its blood mix with the&nbsp;
Holy Water. He then repeated the celebrant’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:53.640 --> 00:17:57.660
circuit in the opposite direction, before&nbsp;
stepping into the center of the stone pillars.&nbsp;

00:17:58.560 --> 00:18:04.860
“Blood for the Old Gods, Water for the New King,”&nbsp;
the assistant recited, pouring the remaining mix&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:04.860 --> 00:18:08.940
of blood and Holy Water over a patch of&nbsp;
salt in the middle of the seven pillars.&nbsp;

00:18:08.940 --> 00:18:12.780
Even though he knew it wasn’t his&nbsp;
place to question the Foundation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:12.780 --> 00:18:19.500
as the 220-Calabasas procedure took place, the&nbsp;
guard couldn’t help but wonder what all this was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:19.500 --> 00:18:27.180
for. It seemed so…ritualistic, like something&nbsp;
deeply religious or even magical. He’d never&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:27.180 --> 00:18:31.020
bought into all that occult mumbo-jumbo,&nbsp;
even while working for the Foundation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:31.020 --> 00:18:37.140
but he had learned not to question anything, even&nbsp;
the strangest and most inexplicable of sights.&nbsp;

00:18:38.340 --> 00:18:45.960
Little did he know that beneath his feet, was an&nbsp;
ancient and unknowable horror. A beast, chained&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:45.960 --> 00:18:51.960
and lying in wait. Contained in a chamber directly&nbsp;
underneath the pillars, sat an impossibly-large&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:51.960 --> 00:18:57.960
creature. Humanoid and obese, its body covered&nbsp;
entirely in scales thicker than armour plating.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:58.560 --> 00:19:03.660
Branch-like horns protruded from its jawless&nbsp;
head, pointing up to chains that hung from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:03.660 --> 00:19:10.440
seven pillars above, each one hooked into the&nbsp;
entity’s back. All but one of the chains was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:10.440 --> 00:19:16.440
broken, a final, withering shackle keeping the&nbsp;
Devourer of Worlds in its underground prison.&nbsp;

00:19:17.280 --> 00:19:23.760
Ever since 1894 BCE, when Erikeshan mystics&nbsp;
imprisoned it, the Devourer has been waiting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:23.760 --> 00:19:29.340
patiently for its inevitable freedom. It knows,&nbsp;
as well as the Foundation, that nothing can be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:29.340 --> 00:19:35.400
done to prevent the final chain from one day&nbsp;
breaking. Even Procedure 220-Calabasas won’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:41.400
keep the creature contained, it’s nothing more&nbsp;
than a smokescreen, an act, designed to create&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:41.400 --> 00:19:47.100
an illusion of active containment and maintain&nbsp;
Foundation morale until a permanent solution&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:47.100 --> 00:19:55.860
can be devised to keep SCP-2317 imprisoned.
Of course, if the guard had known this, it would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:55.860 --> 00:20:00.420
have also explained the need for a one-kiloton&nbsp;
nuclear device as part of this staged ritual.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:01.140 --> 00:20:06.600
Procedure 220-Calabasas has all the components&nbsp;
to trick everyone below the O5 Council,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:06.600 --> 00:20:11.760
emulating religious and occult rituals, the&nbsp;
increased level of security surrounding the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:11.760 --> 00:20:17.580
procedure and its purpose, and telling staff&nbsp;
that any failure to correctly, and completely,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:17.580 --> 00:20:24.540
perform the 220-Calabasas procedure will result&nbsp;
in an XK-Class End of the World Scenario.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:25.440 --> 00:20:30.600
All these elements work together to conceal&nbsp;
the truth: that one day, the Devourer will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:30.600 --> 00:20:37.500
escape and lay waste to our dimension.
Knowledge is power, and maybe knowing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:43.260
too much truly is deadly. Perhaps if the guard&nbsp;
had learned any of this, he’d have understood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:43.260 --> 00:20:48.300
why his predecessor never made it out of&nbsp;
psychological evaluation. Maybe if he had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:48.300 --> 00:20:54.240
questioned the purpose of Procedure 220-Calabasas,&nbsp;
he'd have learned the true nature of SCP-2317,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:55.020 --> 00:21:01.080
and what that doorway kept out. But he was&nbsp;
loyal to the Foundation, through and through.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:01.860 --> 00:21:07.200
As the team finished performing 220-Calabasas&nbsp;
and returned though the wooden door, the guard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:07.200 --> 00:21:14.040
took one last glance over his shoulder at the vast&nbsp;
salt plane. The entire dimension was calm, silent,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:14.700 --> 00:21:20.580
but not peaceful: it was patient. The&nbsp;
entity had waited centuries for its time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:20.580 --> 00:21:26.520
and now all it would take was the breaking&nbsp;
of the seventh and final chain. One day.&nbsp;

00:21:27.480 --> 00:21:33.180
The door was closed behind the guard as he,&nbsp;
the celebrant, the assistant and his fellow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:33.180 --> 00:21:38.580
security officer stepped back through,&nbsp;
their work done and, as far as they knew,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:38.580 --> 00:21:44.100
preventing catastrophe for another day.
Only the Foundation higher-ups,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:44.100 --> 00:21:51.120
the Overseer Council, are aware of the true&nbsp;
danger posed by SCP-2317 and its sole inhabitant.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:52.080 --> 00:21:57.240
Current predictions are that at some point within&nbsp;
the next thirty years, the Devourer of Worlds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:57.240 --> 00:22:03.300
will be freed. Any and all attempts to repair or&nbsp;
recreate the chains holding it in place have so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:03.300 --> 00:22:10.320
far failed. As such, the O5 Council has elected to&nbsp;
continue providing Foundation personnel with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:10.320 --> 00:22:15.960
ignorant hope that Procedure 220-Calabasas&nbsp;
is an effective strategy for containment.&nbsp;

00:22:15.960 --> 00:22:22.320
As we’ve said, sometimes the most interesting&nbsp;
thing about a closed door isn’t where it leads,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:22.320 --> 00:22:30.420
it’s what it keeps out. In the case of SCP-2317,&nbsp;
the unassuming wooden door holds at bay an ancient&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:30.420 --> 00:22:37.980
creature of untold power, that will one day break&nbsp;
free and wreak havoc in our dimension. Nothing the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:37.980 --> 00:22:42.420
Foundation does can prevent it, or keep it&nbsp;
contained behind the Door to Another World,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:43.260 --> 00:22:48.780
and only the Overseer Council knows that&nbsp;
any and all efforts to do so are futile.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:49.860 --> 00:22:55.920
With all that in mind, we can only hope&nbsp;
that the doorway of SCP-2317 stays closed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:56.460 --> 00:22:58.980
at least for a little while longer.

00:22:59.580 --> 00:23:06.240
SCP-173 - It’s one of the most iconic anomalies
ever contained by the SCP Foundation.

00:23:06.240 --> 00:23:12.120
This neck-snapping Site-19 celebrity is known
and feared by everyone who works at the Foundation

00:23:12.120 --> 00:23:15.900
since being contained in 1993, its nubby,&nbsp;

00:23:15.900 --> 00:23:18.720
concrete hands metaphorically,&nbsp;
and quite literally,

00:23:18.720 --> 00:23:20.940
stained with the blood of countless people.

00:23:20.940 --> 00:23:27.180
But this mostly immobile oddity wasn’t always
a resident of Site-19, and the story of how

00:23:27.180 --> 00:23:32.760
exactly it ended up there - and more importantly,
why - is far more ridiculous, insane, and

00:23:32.760 --> 00:23:35.340
downright terrifying than you could ever imagine.

00:23:35.340 --> 00:23:37.680
So buckle up, SCP Fans.

00:23:37.680 --> 00:23:40.800
This is the dramatic tale of how this homicidal&nbsp;

00:23:40.800 --> 00:23:43.920
piece of modern art ended&nbsp;
up at the SCP Foundation’s

00:23:43.920 --> 00:23:45.420
largest containment site.

00:23:45.420 --> 00:23:50.160
To give you an idea of just how weird this
origin story is, we’re gonna have to leap

00:23:50.160 --> 00:23:52.560
forward to the year 2045.

00:23:52.560 --> 00:23:55.320
We know what you’re thinking: Isn’t this
a prequel?

00:23:55.320 --> 00:23:57.120
How can it take place in the future?

00:23:57.120 --> 00:24:00.660
Sit tight, folks, it’ll all make sense in
the end.

00:24:00.660 --> 00:24:06.420
Site-91 is where we lay our scene, under the
watchful eyes of Site Director Dr. James Long,

00:24:06.420 --> 00:24:11.700
a senior researcher with Level 4 Security
Clearance - the second highest at the Foundation.

00:24:11.700 --> 00:24:17.640
Dr. Long had given decades of devotion and
his expertise to the Foundation; he was a

00:24:17.640 --> 00:24:22.320
proud man, who wore his life of service to
the containment cause as a badge of honor.

00:24:22.320 --> 00:24:26.520
After years of dodging death while researching
some of the most dangerous anomalies that

00:24:26.520 --> 00:24:31.560
Site-91 had to offer, he had ascended to the
rank of Site Director which represented the

00:24:31.560 --> 00:24:33.000
culmination of his life’s work.

00:24:33.000 --> 00:24:38.460
And in his new position of power, he’d only
proved himself further - running a tight ship,

00:24:38.460 --> 00:24:41.520
and reducing the number of containment breaches
across the board.

00:24:41.520 --> 00:24:47.400
Nobody could say that Dr. Long wasn’t extremely
talented at his job, which is why he was so

00:24:47.400 --> 00:24:52.440
confused when he received an email from Alexandra
Nala, an Administrative Assistant working

00:24:52.440 --> 00:24:54.480
directly for the O5 Council.

00:24:54.480 --> 00:25:00.000
It was the type of email that no Site Director
ever wanted to receive: Dr. Long was being

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:05.220
told that, with no input or oversight from
him, the majority of Site-91’s anomalies

00:25:05.220 --> 00:25:09.120
were going to be taken to an undisclosed location
for “Safer Containment.”

00:25:09.120 --> 00:25:13.980
The list contained nearly every meaningful
detainee contained on the site, including

00:25:13.980 --> 00:25:16.560
of course, SCP-173.

00:25:16.560 --> 00:25:21.960
This particular anomaly had been contained
at the site for 37 years after being delivered

00:25:21.960 --> 00:25:23.460
there in 2008.

00:25:23.460 --> 00:25:28.740
Dr. Long had devised a perfect method to minimize
containment breaches in that time - creating

00:25:28.740 --> 00:25:32.880
a sprinkler system within the chamber that
washes away the waste products produced by

00:25:32.880 --> 00:25:36.480
173, reducing the need for risky human contact.

00:25:36.480 --> 00:25:38.280
But that didn’t matter.

00:25:38.280 --> 00:25:43.980
Despite Dr. Long’s loyalty and efficacy
in serving the SCP Foundation, the decision

00:25:43.980 --> 00:25:47.340
had already been made, with no chance of reversing
it.

00:25:47.340 --> 00:25:52.740
According to Nala, the motion to remove most
of Site-91’s anomalies had received unanimous

00:25:52.740 --> 00:25:57.480
approval from the O5 Council, and the operations
for the transfer would be commandeered by

00:25:57.480 --> 00:26:02.040
the Department of Extra-Universal Affairs,
headed by Senior Agent Sven Kisch.

00:26:02.040 --> 00:26:05.220
Dr. Long was both upset and confused.

00:26:05.220 --> 00:26:10.200
He was producing some of the best results
across the entire Foundation, so why were

00:26:10.200 --> 00:26:12.060
they taking away all of his anomalies?

00:26:12.060 --> 00:26:15.060
Did someone on the O5 Council have it out
for him?

00:26:15.060 --> 00:26:20.700
Dr. Long replied to Nala, asking if - considering
how severe the relocation operation was going

00:26:20.700 --> 00:26:25.080
to be - whether he could get more information
on where the anomalies were being moved to,

00:26:25.080 --> 00:26:26.040
and why.

00:26:26.040 --> 00:26:29.700
He felt that, at the very least, he was owed
some answers on this.

00:26:29.700 --> 00:26:33.240
Nala and her superiors didn’t feel quite
the same way.

00:26:33.240 --> 00:26:37.620
She replied that Dr. Long sadly didn’t have
the clearance to know any of the operation’s

00:26:37.620 --> 00:26:43.140
particulars - this information was reserved
for those with Level 5 Clearance, and members

00:26:43.140 --> 00:26:44.760
of the Multi-Universal Department.

00:26:44.760 --> 00:26:49.680
All that Dr. Long needed to do was stay out
of the way, and everything would be taken

00:26:49.680 --> 00:26:50.580
care of for him.

00:26:50.580 --> 00:26:52.680
But that wasn’t enough for Dr. Long.

00:26:52.680 --> 00:26:54.660
He needed to know more.

00:26:54.660 --> 00:26:58.980
He needed to understand why this seemingly
random decision had been made.

00:26:58.980 --> 00:27:04.260
Realizing that Nala and the O5 Council were
a dead end as far as information was concerned,

00:27:04.260 --> 00:27:10.380
he instead reached out to the next best thing:
Senior Agent Sven Kisch, the member of the

00:27:10.380 --> 00:27:14.520
Department of Extra-Universal Affairs who
was spearheading the relocation mission.

00:27:14.520 --> 00:27:19.860
Dr. Long implored the Agent to give him extra
information on where all the Site-91 anomalies

00:27:19.860 --> 00:27:23.340
were being moved, and why they were being
moved in the first place.

00:27:23.340 --> 00:27:28.020
Predictably, he was once again stonewalled,
being told that any information regarding

00:27:28.020 --> 00:27:30.240
the project was above his level of clearance.

00:27:30.240 --> 00:27:35.280
In a move that seemed decidedly spiteful,
Agent Kisch signed off by saying that he looked

00:27:35.280 --> 00:27:37.920
forward to seeing Dr. Long at Site-91.

00:27:37.920 --> 00:27:40.500
And not long after that, he did.

00:27:40.500 --> 00:27:45.480
Agent Kisch along with a huge number of agents
and task force members from the Multi-U Department

00:27:45.480 --> 00:27:49.080
arrived on site, bearing state of the art
containment equipment.

00:27:49.080 --> 00:27:54.240
An exasperated Dr. Long wasn’t able to glean
any more information from this experience

00:27:54.240 --> 00:27:59.220
- the Multi-U agents were ruthlessly efficient,
transferring the lion’s share of the anomalies

00:27:59.220 --> 00:28:03.900
into temporary containment and transporting
them off-site within a few hours.

00:28:03.900 --> 00:28:08.760
By the time they were done, Dr. Long and his
staff were left with one of the most desolate

00:28:08.760 --> 00:28:11.820
and empty containment sites on the Foundation’s
books.

00:28:11.820 --> 00:28:17.580
Here was Dr. Long, with decades of service,
and climbing the organizational ladder, only

00:28:17.580 --> 00:28:22.500
to be left as a glorified babysitter for a
handful of low-priority anomalous items.

00:28:22.500 --> 00:28:24.720
It all felt like a cruel joke.

00:28:24.720 --> 00:28:30.720
After several days of nothing happening in
the now-incredibly-uneventful Site-91, a bored

00:28:30.720 --> 00:28:33.720
Dr. Long reached out to a&nbsp;
friend of his - Researcher&nbsp;

00:28:33.720 --> 00:28:37.680
Nurul Shafiqah binte Ahmad Ibrahim, whom he

00:28:37.680 --> 00:28:40.560
called by the nickname Shaq - to vent his
frustrations.

00:28:40.560 --> 00:28:43.500
She commiserated, sharing her sympathy for&nbsp;

00:28:43.500 --> 00:28:46.080
his suddenly much less&nbsp;
exciting working conditions,

00:28:46.080 --> 00:28:49.560
but saying that at least the job should be
a little less lethal now.

00:28:49.560 --> 00:28:54.840
Shaq didn’t know it yet, but on this particular
point, she was terribly wrong.

00:28:54.840 --> 00:28:59.760
Dr. Long shared his theory that perhaps some
sites were being consolidated so the Foundation

00:28:59.760 --> 00:29:02.820
could save money, and that this would lead
to layoffs.

00:29:02.820 --> 00:29:05.820
Shaq essentially told him that he was worrying
too much.

00:29:05.820 --> 00:29:11.160
The reality was that Dr. Long had some very
good reasons to be worried, his problem was

00:29:11.160 --> 00:29:13.980
that he hadn’t been worrying about the right
things.

00:29:13.980 --> 00:29:19.020
In Foundation Containment Area-179, something
awful was brewing.

00:29:19.020 --> 00:29:25.620
As usual, guards posted around SCP-2317 - an
old door containing a portal to another world

00:29:25.620 --> 00:29:30.840
- waited while Foundation staff and D-Classes
performed the standard Procedure 220-Calabasas

00:29:30.840 --> 00:29:31.860
ritual within.

00:29:31.860 --> 00:29:36.840
They were dealing with one of the most dangerous
anomalies in the entire universe, but even

00:29:36.840 --> 00:29:40.980
then, after decades of service, one can become
numb to such things.

00:29:40.980 --> 00:29:45.720
Suddenly, without warning, the door opened
and a terrified Foundation researcher tumbled

00:29:45.720 --> 00:29:49.320
out, panting heavily, eyes bulging in existential
horror.

00:29:49.320 --> 00:29:51.720
He screamed the words that he had long hoped&nbsp;

00:29:51.720 --> 00:29:54.660
would never be spoken in&nbsp;
his or even his children’s

00:29:54.660 --> 00:29:56.340
lifetime, “It happened!

00:29:56.340 --> 00:29:57.540
The chains have broken!

00:29:57.540 --> 00:29:58.920
The Devourer is free!”

00:29:58.920 --> 00:30:05.280
The siren sounded, and an alert spread out
across the entire Foundation database: SCP-2317

00:30:05.280 --> 00:30:11.460
is compromised, SCP-2317-K - the Devourer
of Worlds - is free.

00:30:11.460 --> 00:30:17.880
If the creature escapes Area-179, an XK-Class
End of the World Scenario is basically assured,

00:30:17.880 --> 00:30:22.380
so all efforts will be taken to make sure
that the creature does not escape at any cost.

00:30:22.380 --> 00:30:25.620
And they really did mean any cost.

00:30:25.620 --> 00:30:32.700
The old wooden door of SCP-2317 splintered,
as an immense, scaly hand sprang forth, and

00:30:32.700 --> 00:30:34.860
clawed a wave of devastation through the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:34.860 --> 00:30:35.760
containment
chamber.

00:30:35.760 --> 00:30:40.620
Guards were dispatched in the hundreds with
heavy weaponry to buy some time, firing as

00:30:40.620 --> 00:30:45.480
the Devourer, a beast the size of a mountain
rose from the ground, staring at the terrified

00:30:45.480 --> 00:30:48.840
humans below with its one gigantic red eye.

00:30:48.840 --> 00:30:54.420
It couldn’t even feel the bullets, explosives,
or incendiary and laser weaponry being used

00:30:54.420 --> 00:30:54.900
on it.

00:30:54.900 --> 00:31:00.360
The monster just shrugged it off, and murdered
nearly all its attackers with one swipe of

00:31:00.360 --> 00:31:00.960
its claw.

00:31:00.960 --> 00:31:06.900
In a final desperate act, hoping to kill or
at least slow down the beast, staff at Area-179

00:31:06.900 --> 00:31:11.940
made the ultimate sacrifice, and detonated
the entire on-site nuclear arsenal.

00:31:11.940 --> 00:31:17.100
The explosion disintegrated the entire facility
in an instant, and unleashed a radioactive

00:31:17.100 --> 00:31:19.560
shockwave that carried destruction for miles.

00:31:19.560 --> 00:31:21.420
But it wasn’t enough.

00:31:21.420 --> 00:31:28.080
SCP-2317-K walked out of the mushroom cloud
without a scratch on it, ready to show the

00:31:28.080 --> 00:31:30.840
human world what real destruction meant.

00:31:30.840 --> 00:31:36.120
At this point, the battle was already effectively
lost, but the Foundation refused to go down

00:31:36.120 --> 00:31:36.840
without a fight.

00:31:36.840 --> 00:31:42.180
They dispatched all available mobile task
forces - including Mobile Task Force Nu-7,

00:31:42.180 --> 00:31:47.340
Hammer Down, a heavily-armed, battalion-strength
task force created to combat the biggest and

00:31:47.340 --> 00:31:49.200
most extensive threats imaginable.

00:31:49.200 --> 00:31:53.880
And it wasn’t even just the Foundation - true
existential threats have a way of uniting

00:31:53.880 --> 00:31:59.460
people, as the GOC and even the Chaos Insurgency
temporarily put aside their differences to

00:31:59.460 --> 00:32:01.140
take the fight to the Devourer.

00:32:01.140 --> 00:32:02.820
But would any of it be enough?

00:32:02.820 --> 00:32:07.560
Barrages of cruise missiles and ICBMs did
nothing to halt the Devourer’s assault,

00:32:07.560 --> 00:32:13.380
as it rampaged, destroying towns and cities
at first, then regions, then whole nations.

00:32:13.380 --> 00:32:18.360
Swarms of scrambled jets and helicopters were
knocked out of the sky with casual swipes.

00:32:18.360 --> 00:32:22.740
The creature bulldozed over landscapes teeming
with tanks and heavy artillery vehicles.

00:32:22.740 --> 00:32:28.140
It snapped aircraft carriers in half as it
waded from ocean to ocean, systematically

00:32:28.140 --> 00:32:30.240
destroying everything in its path.

00:32:30.240 --> 00:32:36.060
Even satellite-mounted orbital cannons and
the heavy energy weapons of MTF Tau-5, also

00:32:36.060 --> 00:32:39.480
known as "Samsara", did nothing to faze the
Devourer.

00:32:39.480 --> 00:32:45.900
It was finally coming to fruition: The dreaded
XK Class End of the World Scenario, and none

00:32:45.900 --> 00:32:51.180
of the Foundation’s expertise, advanced
technology, or limitless resources could do

00:32:51.180 --> 00:32:52.500
anything to stop it.

00:32:52.500 --> 00:32:57.060
They aided in evacuation efforts, getting
as many people as they could out of harm’s

00:32:57.060 --> 00:33:02.460
way as the Devourer rampaged and destroyed,
but even that was doing little more than borrowing

00:33:02.460 --> 00:33:02.760
time.

00:33:02.760 --> 00:33:05.880
Eventually, the Devourer would destroy all
of them.

00:33:05.880 --> 00:33:08.280
There would be nothing left.

00:33:08.280 --> 00:33:14.220
And all Dr. James Long could do was watch
helplessly from an almost empty Site-91, waiting

00:33:14.220 --> 00:33:16.260
for the tide of destruction to reach him.

00:33:16.260 --> 00:33:21.300
Of course, other Foundation employees - most
prominently, Senior Agent Sven Kisch and the

00:33:21.300 --> 00:33:23.340
Multi-U Department - had other concerns.

00:33:23.340 --> 00:33:26.400
All they needed to do was archive data for
extraction.

00:33:26.400 --> 00:33:30.420
Extraction to where, you ask, seeing as the
world seems to be at its end here?

00:33:30.420 --> 00:33:37.680
Well, Universe 7392-Epsilon-Blue-Lima, otherwise
known as our universe, circa 1993.

00:33:37.680 --> 00:33:42.420
The Foundation works across the multiverse,
and an XK-Class End of the World Scenario

00:33:42.420 --> 00:33:46.020
in one universe really isn’t necessarily
a problem in others.

00:33:46.020 --> 00:33:50.820
On the orders of the O5 Council, Agent Kisch
and his men are charged with extracting data

00:33:50.820 --> 00:33:55.200
and valuable anomalies like SCP-173 from doomed
universes.

00:33:55.200 --> 00:33:58.260
O5 knew that Dr. Long’s universe - Universe&nbsp;

00:33:58.260 --> 00:34:01.920
5643-Gamma-Orange-Delta -&nbsp;
was due for an apocalyptic

00:34:01.920 --> 00:34:04.260
visit from the Devourer of Worlds any day
now.

00:34:04.260 --> 00:34:08.340
That’s why the Multi-U team went in to extract
everything worth saving.

00:34:08.340 --> 00:34:13.140
Dr. Long and the millions of other Level-4
and below employees of that universe’s Foundation

00:34:13.140 --> 00:34:15.600
were never told of their impending doom.

00:34:15.600 --> 00:34:20.160
After all, that sort of thing could probably
lead to unnecessary stress.

00:34:20.160 --> 00:34:24.600
And what they don’t know won’t hurt them
- until, of course, it does.

00:34:24.600 --> 00:34:31.320
In 1993, these anomalous, doomed universe
SCPs were divided among our universe’s various

00:34:31.320 --> 00:34:32.940
applicable containment sites.

00:34:32.940 --> 00:34:37.260
SCP-173, as you already know, ended up in
Site-19.

00:34:37.260 --> 00:34:42.600
But sadly for the people working there, all
the actual data on this entity’s file was

00:34:42.600 --> 00:34:48.480
lost in translation, so as far as they knew,
173 was little more than a big, weird statue

00:34:48.480 --> 00:34:50.460
with apparently dangerous properties.

00:34:50.460 --> 00:34:56.040
Upon first placing it in its containment chamber
in the Site-19 Euclid Wing, Foundation legend

00:34:56.040 --> 00:35:02.100
Dr. Bright, unaware of just what he had here,
assigned Dr. William Motto to begin research

00:35:02.100 --> 00:35:02.700
on the entity.

00:35:02.700 --> 00:35:06.540
He recommended that the Researcher bring two
D-Classes for testing.

00:35:06.540 --> 00:35:11.160
When Dr. Motto was faced with the anomalous
entity’s blank file, he gave a sigh, and

00:35:11.160 --> 00:35:16.260
began to write something in its description
box: “Moved to Site-19 1993.

00:35:16.260 --> 00:35:19.140
Origin is as of yet unknown…”

00:35:19.140 --> 00:35:20.940
Wasn’t that a delightful little tale?

00:35:20.940 --> 00:35:27.600
Now we know how SCP-173 made its way into
Site-19, and what our own universe may have

00:35:27.600 --> 00:35:29.880
to look forward to in 2045.

00:35:29.880 --> 00:35:35.340
So remember, if you ever see Agent Sven Kisch
planning a transfer of anomalies out of your

00:35:35.340 --> 00:35:41.100
site, maybe consider using some of that PTO,
and maybe consider putting a downpayment on

00:35:41.100 --> 00:35:44.220
a nice, cozy apocalypse bunker over in Iceland…

00:35:44.220 --> 00:35:49.860
Jay and Michael were a pair of urban exploration&nbsp;
YouTubers looking for their big break. You&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:49.860 --> 00:35:53.400
might remember their video exploring the&nbsp;
dead mall on the outskirts of your town,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:53.400 --> 00:35:58.260
or the supposedly “haunted” 1950s&nbsp;
insane asylum out in the styx,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:58.260 --> 00:36:04.920
but you certainly won’t find these videos&nbsp;
anywhere online. After The Incident at SCP - 823,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:04.920 --> 00:36:11.040
all of their content was scrubbed away from even&nbsp;
the most comprehensive internet archives. “Why?”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:11.040 --> 00:36:17.040
you ask. Because these unfortunate urban explorers&nbsp;
decided that their big break would be exploring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:17.040 --> 00:36:22.560
a certain abandoned theme park. And it would&nbsp;
be one of the last decisions they ever made.

00:36:22.560 --> 00:36:28.080
Michael and Jay had heard rumors about the&nbsp;
theme park. Its name was lost to time, as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:28.080 --> 00:36:33.300
was the date of its opening and closing, and the&nbsp;
reason it was even abandoned in the first place.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:33.300 --> 00:36:39.120
Even some of the most hardcore urban explorers&nbsp;
didn’t dare to tread there. Something about it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:39.120 --> 00:36:45.420
a good friend had once told Jay, just didn’t feel&nbsp;
right. Sometimes, if you dare to venture into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:45.420 --> 00:36:51.960
forest near the theme park at night, you can&nbsp;
still hear music. The jolly, piping tunes of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:51.960 --> 00:36:58.680
rides and carnival stands still beckoning. As&nbsp;
if to say, “We’re still here. Come and play.”

00:36:58.680 --> 00:37:00.840
Of course, none of this&nbsp;
frightened Jay and Michael.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:01.380 --> 00:37:05.760
They could already smell the sponsorships&nbsp;
from headlamp and compact camera companies.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:05.760 --> 00:37:10.680
No amount of anxiety would stop them from&nbsp;
making their doomed trip to the so-called&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:10.680 --> 00:37:15.540
“Carnival of Horrors.” It’s a terrible&nbsp;
shame - if they’d listened to the stories&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:15.540 --> 00:37:21.420
of this place about how unnatural and evil it&nbsp;
could be...They might still be alive today.

00:37:21.420 --> 00:37:27.420
Like all the best urban explorers, they arrived&nbsp;
at the woods near the abandoned theme park in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:27.420 --> 00:37:32.520
the dead of night. They ignored the signs warning&nbsp;
them about everything from structural instability,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:32.520 --> 00:37:38.700
to dangerous wild animals, to asbestos.&nbsp;
Nothing would keep them out. Nothing.

00:37:38.700 --> 00:37:43.980
They reached the abandoned theme park not long&nbsp;
after, though it was a mere shell of its former&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:43.980 --> 00:37:49.680
self. During the several decades of abandonment,&nbsp;
nature had reclaimed it. The ferris wheel was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:49.680 --> 00:37:55.200
covered in overgrown ivy and the carnival&nbsp;
stands were blanketed with mold. As the duo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:55.200 --> 00:38:00.000
swept through the grounds with their flashlights&nbsp;
and cameras, they saw a faded sign that bore the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:00.000 --> 00:38:02.940
words “Thriller Chiller” - next to the rusty&nbsp;
skeleton of what had once been the park’s most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:02.940 --> 00:38:06.840
popular roller coaster. They also&nbsp;
took their time to marvel at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:06.840 --> 00:38:11.160
exceptionally creepy-looking Tunnel of&nbsp;
Love, the broken down House of Mirrors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:11.160 --> 00:38:15.960
and a huge, grinning statue of the&nbsp;
park’s former mascot, Happy Hippo.

00:38:15.960 --> 00:38:19.380
This theme park was like something&nbsp;
out of a nightmare, which, naturally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:19.380 --> 00:38:24.420
made it potential video gold. But as the&nbsp;
excited duo wandered further into the park,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:24.420 --> 00:38:29.940
they couldn’t help but notice the quiet,&nbsp;
tinny carnival music. Music that seemed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:29.940 --> 00:38:34.920
be drawing them closer. Michael asked Jay if&nbsp;
he could hear the strange, impossible music,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:34.920 --> 00:38:39.840
and felt a chill creep in when he answered&nbsp;
that he did. Could all of the stories be true?

00:38:39.840 --> 00:38:44.040
They were lost in thought, but their&nbsp;
legs kept moving. They were getting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:44.040 --> 00:38:48.840
closer to something now. They could feel a&nbsp;
presence. And was that music getting louder?

00:38:48.840 --> 00:38:53.880
An instant later, though, another sound&nbsp;
cut through the silence - BANG! BANG!

00:38:53.880 --> 00:38:58.320
It echoed out through the still night&nbsp;
air. Birds flew from their perches&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:58.320 --> 00:39:02.040
in the trees. Jay and Michael&nbsp;
both fell to the ground, dead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:02.040 --> 00:39:07.200
their heads taken off by the fifty caliber rounds&nbsp;
of a highly-trained Mobile Task Force Sniper on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:07.200 --> 00:39:13.020
the payroll of the SCP Foundation. Their recording&nbsp;
equipment, along with their bodies, were taken and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:13.020 --> 00:39:18.600
destroyed. Any trace of them was scrubbed from the&nbsp;
internet. It may seem a little harsh, but a bullet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:18.600 --> 00:39:22.980
to the head is a much kinder fate than what would&nbsp;
have awaited these two if they’d kept walking.

00:39:22.980 --> 00:39:28.320
That’s because the Carnival of Horrors is&nbsp;
no dark fairytale. The rumors are all true,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:28.320 --> 00:39:33.480
and something really is waiting in the dark.&nbsp;
That’s why this abandoned theme park is known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:33.480 --> 00:39:40.980
to the SCP Foundation as SCP - 823, a Euclid&nbsp;
class anomaly with a violent history. What’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:40.980 --> 00:39:45.780
even more unnerving is that the researchers&nbsp;
studying 823 have repeatedly implored the O5&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:45.780 --> 00:39:51.360
Council to increase the park’s classification to&nbsp;
Keter and allocate more resources for containment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:51.360 --> 00:39:56.040
only to be denied. But after you’ve heard&nbsp;
about the horrors that unfolded there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:56.040 --> 00:40:00.180
and the danger it poses, you’ll&nbsp;
probably take the researchers’ side.

00:40:00.180 --> 00:40:06.300
The park is divided into two different zones:&nbsp;
The Yellow Zone and the Red Zone. There are to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:06.300 --> 00:40:09.720
be at least six members of Foundation&nbsp;
personnel present in the Yellow Zone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:09.720 --> 00:40:14.880
at all times to ensure that no civilians&nbsp;
wander in. Our two urban explorers earned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:14.880 --> 00:40:19.320
themselves a death sentence not just by&nbsp;
wandering into the Yellow Zone, but passing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:19.320 --> 00:40:24.720
dangerously close to the Red Zone. This is&nbsp;
the true epicenter of the park’s dangerous,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:24.720 --> 00:40:30.300
anomalous activity. It’s a place so hazardous&nbsp;
that anyone entering, whether they’re a civilian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:30.300 --> 00:40:36.600
or a member of Foundation staff, is to be executed&nbsp;
at a distance by sniper fire without hesitation.

00:40:36.600 --> 00:40:42.480
Once upon a time, though nobody knows exactly&nbsp;
when, there was a theme park that seemed no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:42.480 --> 00:40:47.400
different to any other. Eager children and&nbsp;
thrill-seeking teens arrived by the busload,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:47.400 --> 00:40:52.320
ready to stuff their faces with cotton candy&nbsp;
and corn dogs, and then reverse the process&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:52.320 --> 00:40:58.920
on a vast array of rollercoasters. But even then&nbsp;
during these good times, there was something dark&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:58.920 --> 00:41:05.640
lurking behind the cheerful facade. Little by&nbsp;
little everyone, visitors and employees alike,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:05.640 --> 00:41:11.040
started falling victim to strange and horrific&nbsp;
accidents around the park. Of course, when it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:11.040 --> 00:41:16.800
comes to theme parks, accidents come with the&nbsp;
territory, but none like this. Here are just a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:16.800 --> 00:41:22.440
handful of the horrific and mysterious deaths that&nbsp;
occurred while the park was open. So strap in,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:22.440 --> 00:41:26.940
because just like a roller coaster,&nbsp;
this isn’t for the faint of heart.

00:41:26.940 --> 00:41:31.680
A pair of young lovebirds decided they wanted&nbsp;
to enjoy the romance of the Tunnel of Love.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:31.680 --> 00:41:35.940
The two sat in a swan-shaped boat as&nbsp;
they were ferried through darkened&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:35.940 --> 00:41:41.040
passageways. Anyone would assume that they&nbsp;
were having a great time, but at some point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:41.040 --> 00:41:46.320
terrible shrieks of pain and fear began&nbsp;
to echo through the ride. Attendants,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:46.320 --> 00:41:51.420
confused and terrified, stopped the ride and&nbsp;
found that the screaming persisted. Just some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:51.420 --> 00:41:56.760
stupid teens playing a prank, they figured, and&nbsp;
started the ride again. But when the swan-shaped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:56.760 --> 00:42:01.860
boat finally exited the Tunnel of Love, the&nbsp;
park employees were greeted to a horrifying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:01.860 --> 00:42:07.920
sight: The two teens, dead, their bodies&nbsp;
somehow fused together at multiple points.

00:42:07.920 --> 00:42:13.320
Another unlucky customer met a gruesome fate&nbsp;
inside the House of Mirrors. They entered,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:13.320 --> 00:42:17.400
but while inside, they were stalked&nbsp;
by a mysterious, carnivorous,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:17.400 --> 00:42:24.000
humanoid entity known as Subject 79. The customer&nbsp;
was pursued and eventually caught by Subject 79,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:24.000 --> 00:42:30.000
and brutally dismembered. Some parts of the body&nbsp;
were fused to the House of Mirrors’ interior while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:30.000 --> 00:42:36.060
others - like the right arm - were never found.&nbsp;
This customer actually survived their ordeal - and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:36.060 --> 00:42:40.800
whether that’s a happy ending is up to you.
But it wasn’t just the customers at the park&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:40.800 --> 00:42:46.740
who were in danger. A 23-year-old park employee&nbsp;
working a summer job collapsed while entertaining&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:46.740 --> 00:42:51.900
children dressed as the park’s cheerful mascot,&nbsp;
Happy Hippo. It wasn’t uncommon for people to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:51.900 --> 00:42:57.000
get overheated and collapse in the heavy suits&nbsp;
on hot days, but one thing was different here:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:57.000 --> 00:43:01.920
He was screaming, crying, and trying&nbsp;
desperately to remove his mask.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:01.920 --> 00:43:07.740
People rushed to help, but nobody could get the&nbsp;
suit off, and he was declared dead soon after.

00:43:07.740 --> 00:43:11.520
When he was eventually cut out of&nbsp;
the suit, coroners found that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:11.520 --> 00:43:15.780
employee had choked to death. His mouth,&nbsp;
trachea, and lungs were filled with a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:15.780 --> 00:43:20.280
fibrous substance later determined to be&nbsp;
identical to the stuffing of his costume.

00:43:20.280 --> 00:43:25.260
An intense roller coaster known as the Thriller&nbsp;
Chiller was a magnet for horrific accidents,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:25.260 --> 00:43:30.000
which became more violent and intense&nbsp;
over time. The first accident seemed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:30.000 --> 00:43:34.980
like a typical theme park tragedy - A safety&nbsp;
harness failed dropping a rider fifteen feet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:34.980 --> 00:43:39.900
during an inverted loop. They landed on the&nbsp;
track below, breaking their neck and skull,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:39.900 --> 00:43:44.280
causing instant death. While this&nbsp;
was a tragedy, it wasn’t exactly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:44.280 --> 00:43:49.260
anomalous. But the next major accident on&nbsp;
the ride was an entirely different story.

00:43:49.260 --> 00:43:54.600
This time, fifteen people met with disaster&nbsp;
while riding the Thriller Chiller roller&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:54.600 --> 00:43:59.700
coaster. Starting from the front and moving&nbsp;
back one car at a time, each group of riders was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:59.700 --> 00:44:05.760
decapitated by blunt force trauma. A new pair of&nbsp;
decapitations appeared to happen at every turn and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:05.760 --> 00:44:11.280
loop on the ride. Forensic scientists still have&nbsp;
no idea how this could have possibly occurred.

00:44:11.280 --> 00:44:17.520
Despite all of these disasters, the park was only&nbsp;
finally abandoned after a day known as “Bloody&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:17.520 --> 00:44:24.660
Sunday”, when the anomalous powers of the location&nbsp;
reached a twenty year peak. It’s believed that 231&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:24.660 --> 00:44:30.720
people were killed during the carnage of that day,&nbsp;
and another seven were horribly maimed. The SCP&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:30.720 --> 00:44:35.760
Foundation contained the Carnival of Horrors not&nbsp;
long after, but the mysterious deaths didn’t even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:35.760 --> 00:44:42.060
end there. Foundation Mobile Task Force Rho-71,&nbsp;
also known as the Origami Toads, were sent in to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:42.060 --> 00:44:47.280
assess containment procedures and discover the&nbsp;
source of all the anomalous deaths. They were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:47.280 --> 00:44:53.880
unsuccessful though, and instead they merely added&nbsp;
to the list, in exceptionally horrifying ways.

00:44:53.880 --> 00:44:59.520
One agent was found dead, surrounded by empty&nbsp;
grenades and bullet casings. It appeared he’d&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:59.520 --> 00:45:02.940
removed the explosive propellant from&nbsp;
all of his ballistics and consumed it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:02.940 --> 00:45:08.100
dying in the process. Another was found with&nbsp;
his jaw broken, having apparently pulled out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:08.100 --> 00:45:13.680
and inhaled his own teeth, and dying of the&nbsp;
resulting internal damage. The commander got&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:13.680 --> 00:45:19.620
the worst fate of all - so horrifying, in fact,&nbsp;
that we can’t tell you the full details. All&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:19.620 --> 00:45:24.480
you need to know is that something was shoved&nbsp;
into his brain that really didn’t belong there.

00:45:24.480 --> 00:45:28.740
The Foundation considered having the entire&nbsp;
park destroyed with a massive airstrike,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:28.740 --> 00:45:35.280
courtesy of the Mobile Task Force Nu-7, aka Hammer&nbsp;
Down. However, the O5 Council denied this request,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:35.280 --> 00:45:39.840
on the basis that the park was too close&nbsp;
to populated land, they’d have no plausible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:39.840 --> 00:45:44.340
cover story for the bombing, and they don’t even&nbsp;
really know if blowing up the park would prevent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:44.340 --> 00:45:50.100
anomalous activity from occurring. The Carnival&nbsp;
of Horrors is here to stay, folks, the Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:50.100 --> 00:45:55.980
just hopes to keep it from getting new visitors.
So then back to why the researchers want this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:55.980 --> 00:46:00.960
place upgraded to Keter. After all, these&nbsp;
classifications aren’t about how dangerous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:46:00.960 --> 00:46:07.200
an anomaly is - they’re about how difficult and&nbsp;
complicated they are to contain. But here’s the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:46:07.200 --> 00:46:10.860
problem - according to researchers,&nbsp;
the Red Zone - where the dangerous,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:46:10.860 --> 00:46:17.040
anomalous activity is at its peak - isn’t bound to&nbsp;
one fixed position. It’s changed position at least&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:46:17.040 --> 00:46:23.580
three times already, and even worse, it appears&nbsp;
to be growing. Not seeming so Euclid class now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:46:23.580 --> 00:46:29.100
is it? After all, you might not even need to&nbsp;
visit the Carnival of Horrors to be in grave&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:46:29.100 --> 00:46:35.640
danger. If it keeps growing then someday soon,&nbsp;
the Carnival of Horrors may be visiting you…

00:46:35.640 --> 00:46:41.760
SCP Foundation agents stationed at Area 37
had intercepted chatter from a normally closed

00:46:41.760 --> 00:46:43.680
communication system in a nearby city.

00:46:43.680 --> 00:46:48.960
To anyone else, the calls that the Foundation
were eavesdropping would seem innocent - even

00:46:48.960 --> 00:46:53.460
boring, but the Foundation immediately recognized
the coded language being used.

00:46:53.460 --> 00:46:58.260
They were listening to communications between
underground cells of The Serpent’s Hand

00:46:58.260 --> 00:47:03.900
- a dangerous paramilitary organization that
stands in opposition to everything the Foundation

00:47:03.900 --> 00:47:05.040
is trying to do.

00:47:05.040 --> 00:47:10.440
Once deciphered, the Serpent’s Hand messages
revealed plans for killing Foundation personnel,

00:47:10.440 --> 00:47:15.960
breaking into containment sites, and releasing
anomalous creatures and objects into the world

00:47:15.960 --> 00:47:20.940
- pretty standard stuff for the Foundation’s
least-favorite, anomaly-loving insurgents.

00:47:20.940 --> 00:47:26.160
But they kept using one code that even the
Foundation didn’t have any intel on - they

00:47:26.160 --> 00:47:29.280
kept asking about the condition of The Sisters.

00:47:29.280 --> 00:47:34.860
Fate has a funny way of sneaking up on you
though, and in time, they would know more

00:47:34.860 --> 00:47:40.140
about the powerful, sadistic, reality-warping
beings known as The Sisters than they could

00:47:40.140 --> 00:47:41.400
have possibly imagined.

00:47:41.400 --> 00:47:46.320
But what they would eventually learn was not
the kind of data that anyone would ever want

00:47:46.320 --> 00:47:47.100
to have.

00:47:47.100 --> 00:47:52.740
After intercepting clear lines of communication
from a local Serpent’s Hand cell, triangulating

00:47:52.740 --> 00:47:57.540
the location of their compound was child’s
play, and Mobile Task Forces were dispatched

00:47:57.540 --> 00:48:02.580
from Area 37 with orders to neutralize the
potential threat before they could mount an

00:48:02.580 --> 00:48:03.720
attack on a facility.

00:48:03.720 --> 00:48:09.000
Just when the Serpent’s Hands least expected
it, they had heavily-armed Foundation soldiers

00:48:09.000 --> 00:48:13.800
kicking down their doors, crashing through
windows, and rappelling down from the ceiling.

00:48:13.800 --> 00:48:18.900
As expected, the Serpent’s Hand put up a
fight, but thanks to their superior training

00:48:18.900 --> 00:48:23.760
and the element of surprise, the Foundation’s
Mobile Task Forces came out on top.

00:48:23.760 --> 00:48:28.080
They were able to capture fifteen surviving
members of the group for interrogation, as

00:48:28.080 --> 00:48:31.200
well as a collection of anomalous objects
being stored by the group.

00:48:31.200 --> 00:48:36.240
Among them were a small wooden loom, an enamel
needle, and a glass eye.

00:48:36.240 --> 00:48:41.340
When the task force obtained these seemingly
mundane items, a haunted-looking Serpent’s

00:48:41.340 --> 00:48:43.140
Hand began laughing wildly.

00:48:43.140 --> 00:48:47.580
He kept repeating, “You have no idea what
you’re getting yourselves into...”

00:48:47.580 --> 00:48:50.880
Nobody knew just how right this man was.

00:48:50.880 --> 00:48:52.800
Not yet, anyway.

00:48:52.800 --> 00:48:58.260
Congratulating themselves on a job well done,
the Mobile Task Forces hauled their captives

00:48:58.260 --> 00:49:03.780
and the new anomalous items back to Area 37
- a heavily isolated Foundation site that

00:49:03.780 --> 00:49:08.700
specializes in the early containment of anomalous
objects for initial observation and study.

00:49:08.700 --> 00:49:13.380
The objects hadn’t displayed any anomalous
properties in transit - maybe the Serpent’s

00:49:13.380 --> 00:49:18.420
Hand was lying and these weren’t dangerous
items at all, or it was actually just a pile

00:49:18.420 --> 00:49:18.900
of junk.

00:49:18.900 --> 00:49:23.880
Either way, they were sent to a Foundation
researcher on site to conduct preliminary

00:49:23.880 --> 00:49:24.480
tests.

00:49:24.480 --> 00:49:29.220
The loom, the needle, and the glass eye were
laid out across the table for observation,

00:49:29.220 --> 00:49:34.380
when suddenly, the attending researcher felt
a dark presence looming behind him.

00:49:34.380 --> 00:49:40.320
He turned, with sweat beading on his brow,
and saw three humanoid, translucent figures

00:49:40.320 --> 00:49:42.120
floating in the air behind him.

00:49:42.120 --> 00:49:48.660
They would soon become known as SCP - 1765
One, Two, and Three.

00:49:48.660 --> 00:49:53.460
The researcher could feel the power emanating
from these silhouettes - reality seemed to

00:49:53.460 --> 00:49:58.200
bend and shimmer around them, the way heat
distorts the air into a mirage.

00:49:58.200 --> 00:50:01.800
He could tell right away that they were powerful
reality-warpers.

00:50:01.800 --> 00:50:07.020
Even in their brief time communicating with
the researcher, One, Two, and Three displayed

00:50:07.020 --> 00:50:09.480
both intelligence and unique personalities.

00:50:09.480 --> 00:50:14.040
One was clearly the ringleader - displaying
an articulate command of language.

00:50:14.040 --> 00:50:20.580
Two displayed a more mischievous side, speaking
with a cockney accent and had a tendency towards

00:50:20.580 --> 00:50:21.480
creepy giggling.

00:50:21.480 --> 00:50:26.460
Three was the least communicative of them
all - preferring to speak in short, simple

00:50:26.460 --> 00:50:29.640
sentences, often consisting of just single
words.

00:50:29.640 --> 00:50:35.520
Though of course, actions speak far louder
than words - and it didn’t take long for

00:50:35.520 --> 00:50:38.340
the Sisters to define themselves with their
actions.

00:50:38.340 --> 00:50:43.380
One told the scared and confused researcher
that they’d been observing the SCP Foundation

00:50:43.380 --> 00:50:48.120
for quite some time, and that they deeply
admired the Foundation’s adherence to the

00:50:48.120 --> 00:50:49.020
scientific method.

00:50:49.020 --> 00:50:53.220
Of course, the researcher wasn’t so much
“flattered” by the Sister’s statement

00:50:53.220 --> 00:50:55.740
as they were “afraid for their life.”

00:50:55.740 --> 00:51:00.420
They tried to call security for backup, but
found that their tongue was withering and

00:51:00.420 --> 00:51:03.360
turning into a shrivelled, blackened husk
in their mouth.

00:51:03.360 --> 00:51:06.240
The Sisters didn’t like to be interrupted.

00:51:06.240 --> 00:51:11.100
As the tongueless researcher slowly collapsed
in front of them, the Sisters explained the

00:51:11.100 --> 00:51:15.240
purpose of their visit - They wished to assist
the Foundation in their quest for knowledge,

00:51:15.240 --> 00:51:19.680
and, as such, they would conduct a number
of experiments on their behalf.

00:51:19.680 --> 00:51:24.360
They would then happily share the resulting
data with the Foundation to compare notes.

00:51:24.360 --> 00:51:27.600
One expressed optimism, saying that she believed&nbsp;

00:51:27.600 --> 00:51:30.120
they were about to embark&nbsp;
on a beautiful scientific

00:51:30.120 --> 00:51:30.900
relationship.

00:51:30.900 --> 00:51:34.200
The reality couldn’t be further from the
truth.

00:51:34.200 --> 00:51:39.420
The Sisters began their work, moving rapidly
around the facility, bending and twisting

00:51:39.420 --> 00:51:40.860
reality wherever they went.

00:51:40.860 --> 00:51:45.960
They circled Area 37, marking it as separate
from the rest of the world it inhabited.

00:51:45.960 --> 00:51:51.240
Area 37 no longer belonged to planet earth
- it belonged to the Sisters.

00:51:51.240 --> 00:51:56.700
It was their private experimentation lab,
filled with live and unwilling guinea pigs.

00:51:56.700 --> 00:52:02.160
The Foundation attempted to retake the facility
by force, sending Mobile Task Force Iota-6,

00:52:02.160 --> 00:52:07.080
also known as the Canvas Cats, into the belly
of the beast, but they never returned.

00:52:07.080 --> 00:52:12.060
In addition to changing the fabric of reality
itself, they also altered the physical structure

00:52:12.060 --> 00:52:15.780
of Area 37 to better serve their experimental
designs.

00:52:15.780 --> 00:52:23.640
It was divided into four sections, marked
A, B, C, and D, each with its own unique purpose.

00:52:23.640 --> 00:52:29.640
Section A - which had formerly been Area 37’s
storekeeping, mess hall, and dormitories - had

00:52:29.640 --> 00:52:32.520
been the least affected by the Sisters’
attacks on reality.

00:52:32.520 --> 00:52:37.380
The biggest alterations were the appearance
of two large, metal vats situated in the east

00:52:37.380 --> 00:52:42.600
corner of the mess hall, a monitoring station
connected to other sections of Area 37 that

00:52:42.600 --> 00:52:47.880
replaced the storekeeping zones, and an imposing
marble sign hanging above the dormitories

00:52:47.880 --> 00:52:49.860
that reads “CONTROL GROUP.”

00:52:49.860 --> 00:52:54.660
A quick refresher from science class, the
control group in an experiment is the group

00:52:54.660 --> 00:52:59.100
that isn’t subjected to the experimental
effect the others are, so they can be used

00:52:59.100 --> 00:53:00.720
as a benchmark to measure against.

00:53:00.720 --> 00:53:05.820
The same was true here - the prisoners in
the control group were the safest of all,

00:53:05.820 --> 00:53:10.920
but they were forced to do something almost
as bad, they had to watch the horrors playing

00:53:10.920 --> 00:53:12.720
out across the rest of the facility.

00:53:12.720 --> 00:53:17.160
One of the Sisters would occasionally return
to this section to oversee the feeding of

00:53:17.160 --> 00:53:21.960
the control subjects, and to encourage them
to take part in the observation of their unlucky

00:53:21.960 --> 00:53:22.260
peers.

00:53:22.920 --> 00:53:28.440
Section B - which had formerly been Area 37’s
outer grounds and sports facilities - had

00:53:28.440 --> 00:53:32.520
been transformed into the center of a localized
spatial-temporal abnormality.

00:53:32.520 --> 00:53:37.860
In layman’s terms, this meant that its size,
climate, atmospheric composition, pressure,

00:53:37.860 --> 00:53:42.960
and temporal flow were all subject to constant
changes based on the whims of Sister Number

00:53:42.960 --> 00:53:46.800
One - who oversaw all the experiments performed
in Section B.

00:53:46.800 --> 00:53:54.300
For those unfortunate enough to be trapped
in Section B, SCP-1765-1 was their god.

00:53:54.300 --> 00:53:57.000
But she didn’t subject them to her whims
randomly.

00:53:57.000 --> 00:54:02.880
No, in her own words, the purpose of Section
B was to delve into the effects of repetitive

00:54:02.880 --> 00:54:06.780
action performed under unusual conditions
on the human psyche.

00:54:06.780 --> 00:54:11.640
For example, one experiment was set up to
test the physical and mental fortitude of

00:54:11.640 --> 00:54:15.180
a Researcher, a Field Agent, and a sanitation
worker.

00:54:15.180 --> 00:54:19.620
The trio were confined in a sports center
and ordered to measure the length of every

00:54:19.620 --> 00:54:24.480
single pipe and the angle at which each connected
to others with nothing more than a wrench,

00:54:24.480 --> 00:54:28.020
a ruler, a brown paper pad and a ballpoint
pen.

00:54:28.020 --> 00:54:31.260
The task was an arduous one taking over ten
hours.

00:54:31.260 --> 00:54:35.760
And as soon as the subjects were done, One
restructured the sports center and ordered

00:54:35.760 --> 00:54:37.200
them to perform the task again.

00:54:37.200 --> 00:54:43.980
The same happened another 459 times before
One finally concluded the experiment, leaving

00:54:43.980 --> 00:54:47.280
the subjects with broken bodies and minds
in the aftermath.

00:54:47.280 --> 00:54:52.320
Section C - which had previously been the
facility’s main office block - exhibited

00:54:52.320 --> 00:54:57.300
a similar level of anomalous activity to Section
B, except that it was the domain of the more

00:54:57.300 --> 00:54:59.880
sadistic and mischievous Sister Number Two.

00:54:59.880 --> 00:55:05.280
Her main area of scientific interest was studying
group dynamics and interpersonal relationships

00:55:05.280 --> 00:55:09.840
during extreme conditions&nbsp;
- very extreme conditions.

00:55:09.840 --> 00:55:14.460
For one experiment, the office block had been
transformed into a kind of football stadium,

00:55:14.460 --> 00:55:18.060
with the goal posts removed and replaced by
concrete bunkers.

00:55:18.060 --> 00:55:23.880
The two teams were the captured Serpent Hand
members, and the members of MTF Iota-6, fresh

00:55:23.880 --> 00:55:25.800
off their attempt to retake the site.

00:55:25.800 --> 00:55:31.260
The two groups were forced into a deadly game
with incomprehensible rules - including rising

00:55:31.260 --> 00:55:36.900
platforms and hooded figures throwing fiery
projectiles into the crowd, trying to incinerate

00:55:36.900 --> 00:55:37.380
the players.

00:55:37.380 --> 00:55:42.240
But victory didn’t lead to safety, as the
winners of the game were crushed to death

00:55:42.240 --> 00:55:45.420
with giant metal hammers, just for the fun
of it.

00:55:45.420 --> 00:55:50.460
Two didn’t even try to pretend that this
act had a valid scientific justification.

00:55:50.460 --> 00:55:56.580
Section D - which had once been the facility’s
high-risk containment area - was now the strangest

00:55:56.580 --> 00:55:58.680
and most mysterious section of all.

00:55:58.680 --> 00:56:04.440
Under the charge of the equally peculiar and
enigmatic Sister Number Three, this area appeared

00:56:04.440 --> 00:56:08.220
physically unchanged from its state prior
to the arrival of the Sisters.

00:56:08.220 --> 00:56:12.660
Temporally, however, Section D was the most
warped of them all.

00:56:12.660 --> 00:56:18.360
It existed in a kind of temporal bubble, outside
of the rest of our reality’s timeline, giving

00:56:18.360 --> 00:56:23.460
Three a frightening amount of control over
all that went on in her domain outside of

00:56:23.460 --> 00:56:23.700
time.

00:56:23.700 --> 00:56:28.020
There she was performing the most strange
and incomprehensible experiment of all.

00:56:28.020 --> 00:56:31.140
The subject was the former Site Director of
Area 37.

00:56:31.140 --> 00:56:35.880
He was brought to a table, and asked to choose
between two different flavors of ice cream

00:56:35.880 --> 00:56:37.080
that were presented to him.

00:56:37.080 --> 00:56:40.440
Sounds simple enough, so then why is this
the worst of them all?

00:56:40.440 --> 00:56:43.620
Because the Site Director is caught in a time
loop.

00:56:43.620 --> 00:56:48.240
He’s been choosing between various flavors
of ice cream for over ten thousand hours,

00:56:48.240 --> 00:56:50.520
and he doesn’t even seem to know.

00:56:50.520 --> 00:56:52.260
Three’s only comment on the matter?

00:56:52.260 --> 00:56:53.940
“Delicious.”

00:56:53.940 --> 00:56:57.060
All attempts to liberate&nbsp;
the unfortunate inhabitants&nbsp;

00:56:57.060 --> 00:56:59.580
of Area 37 have failed miserably.

00:56:59.580 --> 00:57:05.460
The Sisters don’t appear to operate on any
form of logic or empathy, and thus, cannot

00:57:05.460 --> 00:57:06.360
be reasoned with.

00:57:06.360 --> 00:57:11.400
With talks having failed and Mobile Task Force
Iota-6’s attempt to retake the site ending

00:57:11.400 --> 00:57:15.900
in disaster, the only solution left was to
create a guarded perimeter around the area,

00:57:15.900 --> 00:57:21.000
using technology like the Scranton Reality
Anchor to fight back against any potential

00:57:21.000 --> 00:57:22.320
escape by the Sisters.

00:57:22.320 --> 00:57:27.240
The Sisters are potentially so dangerous that
if they ever truly set their minds to leaving,

00:57:27.240 --> 00:57:32.400
it’s considered acceptable to detonate the
facility’s on-site nuclear warhead in hopes

00:57:32.400 --> 00:57:34.020
of finally putting a stop to them.

00:57:34.020 --> 00:57:38.940
In the meantime, the Foundation has built
giant external servers for processing the

00:57:38.940 --> 00:57:43.560
vast quantities of research data the Sisters
are constantly sending from their horrifying

00:57:43.560 --> 00:57:44.280
experiments.

00:57:44.280 --> 00:57:49.800
Sadly for the inhabitants of Area 37, their
grim fate continues to this day.

00:57:49.800 --> 00:57:55.200
The experiments never stop, and the subjects
of said experiments seem to be condemned to

00:57:55.200 --> 00:57:58.920
the eternal torment of SCP - 1765.

00:57:58.920 --> 00:58:04.560
In a way, their unwilling sacrifice protects
us all - because if ever the Sisters were

00:58:04.560 --> 00:58:07.740
interested in performing experiments on a
larger sample size…

00:58:07.740 --> 00:58:11.820
Well, all we can do is hope we end up in the
control group.

00:58:11.820 --> 00:58:16.140
It’s a perfect day for a wedding.

00:58:16.140 --> 00:58:21.660
On a warm spring afternoon, a beautiful bride
and a handsome groom are exchanging the special

00:58:21.660 --> 00:58:24.840
rings they had custom designed and made for
each other.

00:58:24.840 --> 00:58:30.180
As they take turns placing the rings on each
other's fingers, a man standing at the end

00:58:30.180 --> 00:58:32.040
of the wedding party steps out of position.

00:58:32.040 --> 00:58:36.600
He approaches the groomsman next to him and
reaches into his jacket, taking out a pair

00:58:36.600 --> 00:58:38.820
of pliers that he hands to the groomsman.

00:58:38.820 --> 00:58:44.280
The groomsman happily takes the tool and then,
without any hesitation, shoves the pliers

00:58:44.280 --> 00:58:47.460
into his mouth and begins removing his teeth
one by one.

00:58:47.460 --> 00:58:52.260
When he is finished, he hands the bloody teeth
to the man along with the pliers.

00:58:52.260 --> 00:58:56.580
The man then goes to the next groomsman who
repeats the same process.

00:58:56.580 --> 00:59:01.740
He continues going down the line until all
of the groomsmen and bridesmaids have removed

00:59:01.740 --> 00:59:05.640
their teeth, seemingly without pain or resistance.

00:59:05.640 --> 00:59:08.340
The man then approaches the bride and groom.

00:59:08.340 --> 00:59:12.660
He hands each of them half of the pile of
teeth, which they gladly accept.

00:59:12.660 --> 00:59:18.480
They then begin to eat the teeth without delay,
seemingly not bothered by the intense damage

00:59:18.480 --> 00:59:21.780
they’re causing to their own teeth and jaws
by doing so.

00:59:21.780 --> 00:59:26.460
The man watches as the groom moves the priest
who was officiating the wedding aside.

00:59:26.460 --> 00:59:32.160
As the entire church looks on in joy, the
groom opens his mouth and the deafening sound

00:59:32.160 --> 00:59:33.780
of cicadas are heard.

00:59:33.780 --> 00:59:40.680
This is only the beginning of what the SCP
Foundation has labeled an SCP-2852 event,

00:59:40.680 --> 00:59:45.900
a terrifying and little understood phenomenon
that is better known by the nickname of the

00:59:45.900 --> 00:59:48.060
anomalous creature responsible for them…

00:59:48.060 --> 00:59:49.380
Cousin Johnny.

00:59:49.380 --> 00:59:54.120
The Foundation had been trying to contain
Cousin Johnny for decades - not that it’d

00:59:54.120 --> 00:59:55.260
ever done them any good.

00:59:55.260 --> 00:59:59.700
Johnny is a Keter-Class anomaly that’s thus
far proven impossible to contain.

00:59:59.700 --> 01:00:04.980
This is an entity so dangerous and volatile
that three different Mobile Task Forces are

01:00:04.980 --> 01:00:11.460
devoted to detecting and disrupting its activities
- MTF Upsilon-36, aka The Party Crashers.

01:00:11.460 --> 01:00:14.820
MTF Upsilon-52, aka Cater Duty.

01:00:14.820 --> 01:00:18.300
And MTF Upsilon-99, aka The Altar Boys.

01:00:18.300 --> 01:00:23.940
But so far all the Foundation has been able
to really do is swoop in afterwards and do

01:00:23.940 --> 01:00:27.300
their best to pick up the pieces of people’s
shattered lives.

01:00:27.300 --> 01:00:32.520
Cousin Johnny has so far been observed to
only operate in the North American subcontinent,

01:00:32.520 --> 01:00:37.740
and only seems to appear at Anglican or Catholic
baptisms, weddings, and funerals.

01:00:37.740 --> 01:00:42.360
However, Foundation operatives charged with
keeping a lid on Cousin Johnny harbor the

01:00:42.360 --> 01:00:47.820
hidden fear that he may one day expand his
hunting grounds, and wreak terror worldwide.

01:00:47.820 --> 01:00:51.120
If Johnny became multinational&nbsp;
or multi denominational,&nbsp;

01:00:51.120 --> 01:00:54.900
his violence, insanity, and pure evil may

01:00:54.900 --> 01:01:01.080
truly become impossible to minimize, so compatible
communities are constantly monitored for increased

01:01:01.080 --> 01:01:06.060
levels of juvenile delinquency, sterility,
domestic violence, and divorce.

01:01:06.060 --> 01:01:11.160
After all this, you’re probably wondering:
Who or what actually is Cousin Johnny, and

01:01:11.160 --> 01:01:13.500
how does he cause so much horrific tragedy?

01:01:13.500 --> 01:01:17.760
At face value, nothing about the appearance
of Cousin Johnny would suggest an anomalous

01:01:17.760 --> 01:01:19.860
nature, or even any sort of danger.

01:01:19.860 --> 01:01:24.600
He appears to be a middle-aged white male,
often with scruffy hair and a beard.

01:01:24.600 --> 01:01:30.120
On a cellular level too, Cousin Johnny appears
all too human, but when you look at his physiology

01:01:30.120 --> 01:01:31.980
it’s a whole different story.

01:01:31.980 --> 01:01:32.880
Cousin Johnny&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:32.880 --> 01:01:37.740
has no identifiable organs whatsoever
- his body is made out of a fibrous muscular

01:01:37.740 --> 01:01:38.280
tissue.

01:01:38.280 --> 01:01:43.440
The only exceptions are his teeth and hair,
which are made of a kind of chitin - a key

01:01:43.440 --> 01:01:48.000
component of insect exoskeletons, such as
those possessed by cicadas.

01:01:48.000 --> 01:01:51.420
Johnny’s eyes are the first clue that something
is off about him.

01:01:51.420 --> 01:01:56.520
From a distance they appear perfectly normal,
but up close, they’re glassy and dead.

01:01:56.520 --> 01:02:00.720
This is because his eyes aren’t actually
attached to any nerves inside his head.

01:02:00.720 --> 01:02:07.140
With no nervous system or vocal chords, Johnny’s
ability to see, move, and talk defy any kind

01:02:07.140 --> 01:02:08.520
of logical explanation.

01:02:08.520 --> 01:02:13.080
His speech will seem completely normal to
the people under his spell, but to anyone

01:02:13.080 --> 01:02:17.640
else, it comes out as complete nonsense, often
described as word salad.

01:02:17.640 --> 01:02:22.740
If people in attendance are briefed in advance
about this phenomenon, whatever hypnotic ability

01:02:22.740 --> 01:02:27.480
causes them to hear his sounds as intelligible
words won’t work, and they’ll be aware

01:02:27.480 --> 01:02:29.280
of how nonsensical it all sounds.

01:02:29.280 --> 01:02:32.700
But of course, that doesn’t mean they’re
safe.

01:02:32.700 --> 01:02:37.380
Cousin Johnny appears at family gatherings
and religious rituals, and immediately, he’ll

01:02:37.380 --> 01:02:39.540
be treated as though he’s always been there.

01:02:39.540 --> 01:02:41.160
You know your Cousin Johnny, right?

01:02:41.160 --> 01:02:42.900
You go way back.

01:02:42.900 --> 01:02:45.360
Or at least, you’re pretty sure you do.

01:02:45.360 --> 01:02:48.540
Nothing will appear unnatural about his sudden
presence.

01:02:48.540 --> 01:02:53.340
In fact, if you’re one of the victims of
one of his incidents, chances are, you’ll

01:02:53.340 --> 01:02:56.100
actually find yourself taking a shine to Cousin
Johnny.

01:02:56.100 --> 01:03:01.260
Sure his sense of humor is a little crude
and raunchy, but you can’t help but enjoy

01:03:01.260 --> 01:03:01.860
his company.

01:03:01.860 --> 01:03:05.760
He’s a fun guy to be around, and after all,
he’s family!

01:03:05.760 --> 01:03:11.160
As previously mentioned, he’ll only appear
at three different kinds of events: Baptisms,

01:03:11.160 --> 01:03:15.480
Weddings, and Funerals, and only at those
that are affiliated with either the Catholic

01:03:15.480 --> 01:03:16.860
or Anglican religions.

01:03:16.860 --> 01:03:22.320
The SCP Foundation has classified baptisms
that Cousin Johnny attends as Blue Level Events,

01:03:22.320 --> 01:03:27.480
Weddings are known as White Level Events,
and Funerals are Black Level Events - with

01:03:27.480 --> 01:03:31.200
each one escalating in severity, violence,
and horror.

01:03:31.200 --> 01:03:34.440
First, Baptisms - the Blue Level Events.

01:03:34.440 --> 01:03:39.780
In these events, Cousin Johnny will appear
and begin to act as a third godparent, despite

01:03:39.780 --> 01:03:41.640
there traditionally only being two.

01:03:41.640 --> 01:03:46.620
As the infant is lowered into the holy water,
the entirety of their top layer of skin will

01:03:46.620 --> 01:03:48.300
come off, like a molting snake.

01:03:48.300 --> 01:03:52.500
Despite looking horrific, this apparently
causes no harm to the child.

01:03:52.500 --> 01:03:57.120
The godparents will then eat this discarded
skin, as though it’s the most normal thing

01:03:57.120 --> 01:03:57.720
in the world.

01:03:57.720 --> 01:04:02.580
After this, the family will leave the church
together, and Cousin Johnny will leave with

01:04:02.580 --> 01:04:02.760
them.

01:04:02.760 --> 01:04:06.451
He won’t appear at any subsequent celebrations
of the child’s baptism.

01:04:06.451 --> 01:04:06.540
If this is where it ended, it’d be extremely
gross - but not exactly a living nightmare.

01:04:06.540 --> 01:04:10.140
Of course this is just the beginning of the
terror.

01:04:10.140 --> 01:04:14.220
Following Cousin Johnny’s appearance at
the baptism, the child’s risk of dying in

01:04:14.220 --> 01:04:19.380
the next six months skyrockets, and if they
survive, they’re at an increased risk of

01:04:19.380 --> 01:04:22.260
becoming unstable and violent later on in
life.

01:04:22.260 --> 01:04:27.120
Their parents and godparents will both become
unable to conceive any further children, and

01:04:27.120 --> 01:04:30.840
are likely to be found dead from drowning
within five years of the event.

01:04:30.840 --> 01:04:36.180
Those who were only tangentially involved
in the baptism ritual have a massively increased

01:04:36.180 --> 01:04:41.280
chance of failed pregnancies, or - if they
do conceive - they may become a danger to

01:04:41.280 --> 01:04:42.240
their offspring.

01:04:42.240 --> 01:04:46.920
Children who live through Blue Level Events
and survive past adolescence, will experience

01:04:46.920 --> 01:04:51.660
adverse side effects when encountering the
songs of cicadas well into adulthood - from

01:04:51.660 --> 01:04:55.440
experiencing physical sickness to going through
dangerous psychotic episodes.

01:04:55.440 --> 01:04:59.760
Weddings, or White Level Events, are more
complex and severe.

01:04:59.760 --> 01:05:04.740
In this case, Cousin Johnny will insert himself
into the wedding as a groomsman, and the most

01:05:04.740 --> 01:05:08.880
horrifying events will begin to take place
after the vows have been exchanged.

01:05:08.880 --> 01:05:13.380
Johnny will provide various implements that
allow the bridesmaids and groomsmen to remove

01:05:13.380 --> 01:05:18.720
their teeth, which are then given to the bride
and groom to eat - which they do, causing

01:05:18.720 --> 01:05:21.300
severe damage to their own teeth in the process.

01:05:21.300 --> 01:05:27.780
The groom will then vocalize an unknown cicada
call at an incredible volume, as loud as 140

01:05:27.780 --> 01:05:33.060
decibels in some instances, rendering the
bride and everyone else near the altar completely

01:05:33.060 --> 01:05:33.540
deaf.

01:05:33.540 --> 01:05:37.680
At the wedding reception, where everyone is
continuing to behave as if northing out of

01:05:37.680 --> 01:05:42.420
the ordinary is happening, Cousin Johnny will
ruin things further by giving the best man’s

01:05:42.420 --> 01:05:42.840
speech.

01:05:42.840 --> 01:05:47.100
The speech is more of his typical complete
nonsense, though if you’re there you’ll

01:05:47.100 --> 01:05:51.600
never realize this, and think that this is
the best speech you’ve ever heard, with

01:05:51.600 --> 01:05:55.500
some in the audience laughing hysterically
while others cry uncontrollably.

01:05:55.500 --> 01:05:59.280
Once his speech is done, he’ll present a
gift to the newly married couple…

01:05:59.280 --> 01:06:05.280
3.5 kilograms of human hair in various colors,
13 deceased specimens of a certain cicada

01:06:05.280 --> 01:06:09.660
known as Linne's cicada, and 23 human teeth
in a cardboard box.

01:06:09.660 --> 01:06:13.800
DNA tests on all gifts have been inconclusive
as to their origin.

01:06:13.800 --> 01:06:18.780
Much like many celebrity marriages, unions
that occurred during White Level events never

01:06:18.780 --> 01:06:24.360
last, and all end up divorced within two years
- often as a result of domestic violence,

01:06:24.360 --> 01:06:28.920
and any children born during their brief marriage
will be violent and unstable.

01:06:28.920 --> 01:06:33.060
But it’s not just the wedding party that
gets to experience the fun of a visit from

01:06:33.060 --> 01:06:33.660
Cousin Johnny.

01:06:33.660 --> 01:06:38.100
All married individuals who attended the wedding
will find that they are unable to conceive

01:06:38.100 --> 01:06:41.640
children, despite no biological indicators
of infertility.

01:06:41.640 --> 01:06:46.140
Any children present at the White Level Event
will show no interest in romance throughout

01:06:46.140 --> 01:06:50.460
their life, and often die tragically before
reaching the age of eighteen.

01:06:50.460 --> 01:06:55.920
Finally, and most horrifying of all, are funerals
- or Black Level Events.

01:06:55.920 --> 01:07:00.600
While Blue and White Level Events can potentially
be disrupted before they are completed, lessening

01:07:00.600 --> 01:07:05.940
or preventing the horrific results, there
is as yet no way to stop or prevent a Black

01:07:05.940 --> 01:07:07.860
Level Event at any stage.

01:07:07.860 --> 01:07:12.540
Any attempts to prevent Cousin Johnny from
entering the church or funeral home will lead

01:07:12.540 --> 01:07:14.220
to him simply manifesting inside.

01:07:14.220 --> 01:07:19.380
Once in the room where the funeral is taking
place, Cousin Johnny will first take up the

01:07:19.380 --> 01:07:23.880
role of eulogizer and begin speaking his standard
nonsense to the attendants.

01:07:23.880 --> 01:07:28.500
The person who was emotionally closest to
the departed will then open the casket, if

01:07:28.500 --> 01:07:32.940
this was not already an open casket funeral,
and will then produce a large knife.

01:07:32.940 --> 01:07:37.020
It’s unknown where the knives come from
as they’re not present before the event

01:07:37.020 --> 01:07:38.460
and they disappear after.

01:07:38.460 --> 01:07:43.740
The funeral attendees will then use the knife
on their wrists and sometimes throats, draining

01:07:43.740 --> 01:07:45.300
their blood into the coffin.

01:07:45.300 --> 01:07:51.060
Many lose more than enough blood to result
in death, but none ever die from this, nor

01:07:51.060 --> 01:07:54.060
do they seem to feel any pain from their wounds.

01:07:54.060 --> 01:07:59.040
As the attendees take turns bleeding into
the coffin, Cousin Johnny continues his eulogy

01:07:59.040 --> 01:08:04.320
which eventually evolves into a cicada song,
the kind sung by Linne’s cicada males.

01:08:04.320 --> 01:08:08.820
The attendants sing the same song back to
him in a kind of call and response.

01:08:08.820 --> 01:08:13.620
Cousin Johnny will then approach the coffin
and vomit in a mixture of blood, wood pulp,

01:08:13.620 --> 01:08:14.940
and dead cicadas.

01:08:14.940 --> 01:08:19.980
The funeral will then proceed as normal, and
the blood, vomit, and cicada filled casket

01:08:19.980 --> 01:08:22.860
is then taken to the cemetery and buried.

01:08:22.860 --> 01:08:27.540
Black Level Events will usually end with the
body being interred in the ground, but if

01:08:27.540 --> 01:08:31.740
there’s a wake after the funeral, the horrors
of the Black Level Event will continue.

01:08:31.740 --> 01:08:37.080
At the wake, Cousin Johnny will climb on top
of a table, lie down, and encourage the other

01:08:37.080 --> 01:08:42.780
attendants to devour him, which they do - all
while he continues to talk his nonsense.

01:08:42.780 --> 01:08:45.240
Until there is nothing left.

01:08:45.240 --> 01:08:50.820
Much like Blue and White Level events, being
in attendance leads to horrific after-effects.

01:08:50.820 --> 01:08:55.140
All participants who experience this event
will separate from their family through either

01:08:55.140 --> 01:08:57.720
suicide, moving, or divorce.

01:08:57.720 --> 01:09:02.520
Every individual present at the event will
also find that they are no longer able to

01:09:02.520 --> 01:09:07.380
produce offspring, and couples present may
also fall victim to incidences of domestic

01:09:07.380 --> 01:09:13.140
violence, often involving cannibalism, that
usually leave one or both participants dead,

01:09:13.140 --> 01:09:18.120
while six out of ten children involved will
attempt to murder one or both of their parents

01:09:18.120 --> 01:09:20.100
before they turn eighteen.

01:09:20.100 --> 01:09:25.380
These Black Level Events are so horrible for
all involved, that any members of the specialized

01:09:25.380 --> 01:09:30.000
Cousin Johnny Mobile Task Forces that happen
to witness such an event are treated with

01:09:30.000 --> 01:09:35.280
Class-A amnestics before they are transferred
to another task force or retire, to ensure

01:09:35.280 --> 01:09:38.460
that they don’t have to live with the memories
of what they saw.

01:09:38.460 --> 01:09:43.500
Prior to that, they are closely monitored
for any strange or anti-social behavior to

01:09:43.500 --> 01:09:45.240
make sure they weren’t affected by the event.

01:09:45.240 --> 01:09:50.520
And they aren’t the only SCP Foundation
staff at risk of having been impacted by Cousin

01:09:50.520 --> 01:09:50.700
Johnny.

01:09:50.700 --> 01:09:55.800
It is theorized that as many as a third of
Catholic and Anglican D-Class personnel were

01:09:55.800 --> 01:10:01.380
involved in a Black-Level event at some point,
and were driven to madness and violence by

01:10:01.380 --> 01:10:05.700
their fateful brushes with the strange relative
that no one knows.

01:10:05.700 --> 01:10:10.740
So next time you’re at a baptism, or a wedding,
or a funeral, stay vigilant.

01:10:10.740 --> 01:10:12.660
Keep an eye on the other guests.

01:10:12.660 --> 01:10:17.460
And always ask yourself: Do you really have
a Cousin Johnny?

01:10:17.460 --> 01:10:22.140
You hear their footsteps coming down&nbsp;
the halls. Or are those your own?&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:10:22.140 --> 01:10:27.420
Can you even tell the difference? You can tell&nbsp;
they’re getting closer and you can feel the hate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:10:27.420 --> 01:10:32.640
the rage. You turn, shaking, and&nbsp;
finally see them standing right&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:10:32.640 --> 01:10:37.860
in front of you. But in that moment, you&nbsp;
might as well be looking into a mirror.

01:10:37.860 --> 01:10:44.520
And who knows? Perhaps you are. You just don’t&nbsp;
seem to remember having so many reflections...

01:10:44.520 --> 01:10:48.360
Have you ever heard the saying “You&nbsp;
are your own worst enemy?” Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:10:48.360 --> 01:10:54.840
it isn’t usually meant literally. But what if it&nbsp;
was? What if you had to fight a monster…that was&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:10:54.840 --> 01:11:00.000
you? All of your flaws are reflected back&nbsp;
at you. Your strengths, your weaknesses,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:11:00.000 --> 01:11:05.640
your deepest fears, with no way to escape&nbsp;
except a battle to the death. Either way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:11:05.640 --> 01:11:11.640
you’re not making it out alive. It’s just a&nbsp;
matter of which version of you survives. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:11:11.640 --> 01:11:18.180
this isn’t a thought experiment. No, according to&nbsp;
the findings of the SCP Foundation, it’s very much&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:11:18.180 --> 01:11:25.560
a reality. There is a place where this nightmare&nbsp;
comes to life, and it is known as SCP-1919.

01:11:25.560 --> 01:11:32.160
SCP-1919 is a hotel and converted mansion, built&nbsp;
in the early 20th century. From the outside,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:11:32.160 --> 01:11:34.920
it looks pretty much like it&nbsp;
did when it was first built,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:11:34.920 --> 01:11:39.720
and it almost looks like a comfortable&nbsp;
place to stay… if you ignore the eastern&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:11:39.720 --> 01:11:42.600
side of the building that has&nbsp;
sunk partially into the ground.

01:11:42.600 --> 01:11:50.160
The inside, however, is a different story, where&nbsp;
it’s clear the ravages of time have taken their&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:11:50.160 --> 01:11:56.520
toll. The floorboards and ceilings are rotting,&nbsp;
collapsing in on themselves, and the rooms are&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:11:56.520 --> 01:12:02.520
filled with debris. It’s deadly enough to explore&nbsp;
the hotel for these reasons alone, but this is&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:12:02.520 --> 01:12:08.100
only the beginning of the danger for a person&nbsp;
inside. In order to determine just how dangerous&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:12:08.100 --> 01:12:14.100
it is for either one person or group to enter the&nbsp;
structure, the SCP Foundation planned a series of&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:12:14.100 --> 01:12:19.380
research expeditions into the abandoned building,&nbsp;
led by Foundation scientist Dr. Limkiewicz.

01:12:19.380 --> 01:12:24.720
The first expedition seemed relatively&nbsp;
normal, at least it did at the start. A&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:12:24.720 --> 01:12:29.940
39-year-old Caucasian D-Class male known as&nbsp;
D7 was sent into the structure with a camera&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:12:29.940 --> 01:12:36.240
and a communications system, guided remotely by&nbsp;
Dr. Limkiewicz, or Dr. L, and another operative,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:12:36.240 --> 01:12:43.200
a former head of the MTF Tau-11 “Youth Hostiles”&nbsp;
who is referred to in this file only as T11.

01:12:43.200 --> 01:12:47.820
When he arrived at the building, D7 was&nbsp;
unable to get inside through the front&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:12:47.820 --> 01:12:52.560
door or windows. After several minutes of&nbsp;
trial and error, he was finally able to&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:12:52.560 --> 01:12:57.420
get in through the western entrance. Dr. L&nbsp;
picked up a strange, high-pitched whistling&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:12:57.420 --> 01:13:02.700
noise upon D7’s entrance into the building,&nbsp;
but it quickly faded away and was disregarded&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:13:02.700 --> 01:13:08.340
by T11. D7 discovered a torn painting, a&nbsp;
portrait of a young woman with red hair.

01:13:08.340 --> 01:13:13.080
Next to the portrait, shallow scratches&nbsp;
could be seen in the wall, the floor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:13:13.080 --> 01:13:19.020
and parts of the ceiling. Suddenly, D7 ducked&nbsp;
into a hiding place, alarmed. He, and the other&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:13:19.020 --> 01:13:25.320
two operatives listening to his audio feed could&nbsp;
hear heavy breathing… and it didn’t belong to D7.

01:13:25.320 --> 01:13:29.880
Dr. L recommended that D7 evacuate the&nbsp;
building at this sign of another entity&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:13:29.880 --> 01:13:35.640
inside, but T11 overruled, ordering him to&nbsp;
disregard that instruction and continue his&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:13:35.640 --> 01:13:41.100
investigation. D7 was told to stay at a safe&nbsp;
distance from whatever was inside with him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:13:41.100 --> 01:13:46.680
and attempt to capture it on video. D7 turned&nbsp;
off his flashlight in order to better hide, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:13:46.680 --> 01:13:52.260
T11 commanded that he turn it back on. Whatever&nbsp;
was caught in its beam of light was difficult for&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:13:52.260 --> 01:13:57.900
the camera to see, but it threw D7 into a panic&nbsp;
and he began to run in the opposite direction.

01:13:57.900 --> 01:14:03.360
When prompted to explain what he&nbsp;
saw, D7 simply said: “It was me!”

01:14:03.360 --> 01:14:09.000
D7 ran through the dark, panting with fear&nbsp;
and exertion. Unable to see where his feet&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:14:09.000 --> 01:14:12.540
were landing, he tripped over something&nbsp;
and came crashing onto the ground,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:14:12.540 --> 01:14:17.820
dropping the video camera. This allowed the&nbsp;
observing officers to finally see what D7&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:14:17.820 --> 01:14:23.340
was so frightened by, and it became&nbsp;
clear just why D7 was so terrified.

01:14:23.340 --> 01:14:29.340
A man, identical looking to D7, approached from&nbsp;
the end of the hallway, making its way toward&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:14:29.340 --> 01:14:34.560
the real D7. It was followed by another&nbsp;
man who also resembled D7, and another,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:14:34.560 --> 01:14:38.700
all running toward the original.&nbsp;
They all looked exactly like him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:14:38.700 --> 01:14:42.660
with a few notable differences. They&nbsp;
were dressed in the same uniform,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:14:42.660 --> 01:14:48.000
with the same build and the same features,&nbsp;
but each had something slightly off about him.

01:14:48.000 --> 01:14:51.840
One was missing eyelids,&nbsp;
another had malformed hands,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:14:51.840 --> 01:14:56.460
and the third had its lips fused together&nbsp;
into a fleshy mass beneath its nose.

01:14:56.460 --> 01:15:02.160
Dr. L moved to cut the camera feed, but T11&nbsp;
demanded that it be kept running. D7 couldn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:02.160 --> 01:15:07.620
be seen by the camera, but the microphone picked&nbsp;
up the sounds of flesh and cloth being torn, along&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:07.620 --> 01:15:13.500
with pained, panicked screams as the duplicates&nbsp;
set upon him. After a moment, the screaming&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:13.500 --> 01:15:18.840
stopped. Two hours later, the camera was broken,&nbsp;
and the expedition brought to a troubling end.

01:15:18.840 --> 01:15:24.120
This was the Foundation’s first glimpse&nbsp;
at the creatures inside of SCP-1919,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:24.120 --> 01:15:29.700
and it was not pretty. It did, however, allow them&nbsp;
to begin understanding the nature of the building,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:29.700 --> 01:15:34.980
and what happens when a person goes inside.&nbsp;
It appears that when a human enters the hotel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:34.980 --> 01:15:40.200
several humanoid creatures manifest throughout the&nbsp;
building. These creatures look like the subject,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:40.200 --> 01:15:45.420
and are equipped with the same clothing or items&nbsp;
that the subject brought inside with them. Though&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:45.420 --> 01:15:51.060
they are nearly mirror images of the subject, they&nbsp;
are always slightly warped in a variety of ways.

01:15:51.060 --> 01:15:56.700
These have included changes to limb and digit&nbsp;
length, joint mobility, sealed nostrils,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:56.700 --> 01:16:01.740
lengthened jaws hanging loose and limp,&nbsp;
missing eyelids, and lips that are fused&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:01.740 --> 01:16:06.300
together. These creatures are highly aggressive&nbsp;
toward the structure of the building itself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:06.300 --> 01:16:12.060
as well as to the subject that they resemble.&nbsp;
They do not, however, attack each other. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:12.060 --> 01:16:17.100
appear to operate with a hive mind, exhibiting&nbsp;
swarm intelligence like that of an ant colony.

01:16:17.100 --> 01:16:19.560
Once they have been spawned by&nbsp;
the entrance of a new person,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:19.560 --> 01:16:24.420
they will not stop until said person&nbsp;
either escapes the building or is killed.

01:16:24.420 --> 01:16:28.080
After the unfortunate end to the first&nbsp;
expedition, the Foundation prepped for&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:28.080 --> 01:16:34.980
a second trip inside. This time, three men were&nbsp;
sent in with Dr. L’s guidance, known as D3, D4,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:34.980 --> 01:16:40.980
and D9. Video cameras were sewn into their clothes&nbsp;
to leave their hands free and to help avoid some&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:40.980 --> 01:16:45.480
of the issues that came up during the first&nbsp;
expedition. This small team was sent in with&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:45.480 --> 01:16:51.060
the orders to terminate the remaining copies of&nbsp;
D7, and further examine the hotel’s interior.

01:16:51.060 --> 01:16:56.160
Upon opening the door to the building, they&nbsp;
were immediately attacked by one of D7’s copies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:56.160 --> 01:17:00.840
which D9 was able to quickly dispatch&nbsp;
by firing his weapon at its head. Next,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:00.840 --> 01:17:04.860
after a great deal of reluctance,&nbsp;
the three men entered the building&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:04.860 --> 01:17:09.960
where they spotted something unusual&nbsp;
inside. Dr. L was horrified when the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:09.960 --> 01:17:14.700
camera feed revealed seventeen discarded&nbsp;
video cameras spread across the floor.

01:17:14.700 --> 01:17:17.640
They didn’t have much time to&nbsp;
react to this new discovery,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:17.640 --> 01:17:22.860
however, because two doubles, one&nbsp;
mirroring D7 and another mirroring D9,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:22.860 --> 01:17:27.480
emerged from the wall and began to attack.&nbsp;
Dr. L ordered the team to take shelter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:27.480 --> 01:17:31.320
then called the team of guards outside of&nbsp;
the hotel’s perimeter. They were ordered&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:31.320 --> 01:17:35.940
to begin an immediate full perimeter lockdown,&nbsp;
preventing the doubles from leaving the hotel.

01:17:35.940 --> 01:17:41.340
D3, D4, and D9 attempted to make their&nbsp;
way to a safe corner of the building,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:41.340 --> 01:17:47.820
but found themselves met with a murderous double&nbsp;
at every turn. At this point, Dr. L began to hear&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:47.820 --> 01:17:52.560
an unusual sound over the microphone feed, a&nbsp;
high-pitched whine like that of a dentist’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:52.560 --> 01:17:58.080
drill. The operatives on the ground couldn’t hear&nbsp;
a thing, but on Dr. L’s end it was deafening.

01:17:58.080 --> 01:18:02.940
As the team proceeded deeper into the hotel,&nbsp;
they became overcome with a strange feeling&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:02.940 --> 01:18:07.860
of foreboding. Dr. L ordered them to turn&nbsp;
on their flashlights, but they refused and&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:07.860 --> 01:18:13.860
begged Dr. L to keep quiet. When prompted&nbsp;
to explain, D9 said: “she can hear you.”

01:18:13.860 --> 01:18:17.460
The operatives stopped responding,&nbsp;
but their camera feeds caught a faint,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:17.460 --> 01:18:21.000
glowing white light coming from&nbsp;
beneath a door. The door opened,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:21.000 --> 01:18:25.260
and the light flooded the camera, making&nbsp;
the images it captured hard to decipher.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:25.260 --> 01:18:30.120
Just a few frames of a quick-moving female&nbsp;
silhouette were captured before the cameras&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:30.120 --> 01:18:37.260
cut to static. The bodies of D3, D4, and D9&nbsp;
were never recovered, nor were their cameras.

01:18:37.260 --> 01:18:43.500
A third expedition was also sent into SCP-1919,&nbsp;
but very little is known about what occurred&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:43.500 --> 01:18:48.660
during it. The video transcript is highly&nbsp;
classified and only those present for its events,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:48.660 --> 01:18:56.520
or approved to research SCP-1919, have access&nbsp;
to it. An update to the SCP-1919 file following&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:56.520 --> 01:19:00.960
Expedition Three though, indicates that&nbsp;
new information was revealed about the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:00.960 --> 01:19:06.480
hotel during the excursion. According to the&nbsp;
file update, there is some kind of being at&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:06.480 --> 01:19:12.300
the center of the location which is causing all&nbsp;
of the other creatures, the doubles, to appear.

01:19:12.300 --> 01:19:17.820
The only information available about this&nbsp;
being is the use of the word “her” in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:17.820 --> 01:19:23.640
official Foundation log about SCP-1919. This&nbsp;
seems to match up with the last moments of&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:23.640 --> 01:19:29.280
the operatives in Expedition Two, when they&nbsp;
told Dr. L that “she can hear you” and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:29.280 --> 01:19:33.900
few frames of a female figure that were&nbsp;
captured by their cameras. Nothing else&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:33.900 --> 01:19:38.220
is known that has been made available&nbsp;
to anyone outside a very select few.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:38.220 --> 01:19:43.560
Only the original report exists, and all&nbsp;
other copies of it have been destroyed.

01:19:43.560 --> 01:19:48.480
The Foundation has undertaken special containment&nbsp;
procedures to make sure that none of the entities&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:48.480 --> 01:19:53.820
from inside the hotel escape, whether they are&nbsp;
the “evil twins” spawned by humans entering&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:53.820 --> 01:19:59.640
the building, or the mysterious female being at&nbsp;
the center of the entire disturbing phenomenon.

01:19:59.640 --> 01:20:05.340
The Foundation has classified SCP-1919&nbsp;
as Euclid and a two kilometer radius&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:05.340 --> 01:20:11.640
must be maintained around SCP-1919, with all&nbsp;
roads leading to the building are blocked or&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:11.640 --> 01:20:16.620
diverted so that no vehicles are able to&nbsp;
reach it. This perimeter is guarded by a&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:16.620 --> 01:20:21.600
set of at least forty armed and armored guards&nbsp;
at any given time. As it has been determined&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:21.600 --> 01:20:26.400
that the doubles spawned by 1919 are equipped&nbsp;
with whatever the human they are copying has,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:26.400 --> 01:20:31.800
no one is allowed to enter the hotel&nbsp;
with body armor or weapons of any kind.

01:20:31.800 --> 01:20:36.780
Anyone that approaches the perimeter that is&nbsp;
not part of an official expedition team will&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:36.780 --> 01:20:41.880
be immediately terminated. No new expeditions&nbsp;
teams are allowed to enter the building unless&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:41.880 --> 01:20:46.980
all doubles from the previous expedition&nbsp;
have been exterminated. In the event that&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:46.980 --> 01:20:51.600
they cannot be exterminated, enough time&nbsp;
must elapse between expeditions that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:51.600 --> 01:20:55.560
previous doubles have starved to death.&nbsp;
Though they do not seem to feel hunger,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:55.560 --> 01:21:00.660
the doubles do need to eat to survive, and&nbsp;
will die when left alone for long enough.

01:21:00.660 --> 01:21:07.320
SCP-1919 has been sealed off from the rest of&nbsp;
the world, so that no hapless civilians can&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:21:07.320 --> 01:21:12.900
wander inside and find themselves torn to&nbsp;
pieces by warped images of themselves. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:21:12.900 --> 01:21:17.820
that comfort turns cold when you realize that&nbsp;
the SCP Foundation still does not understand&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:21:17.820 --> 01:21:23.700
what causes these doubles to spawn. Is it&nbsp;
scientific? Supernatural? Or something else?

01:21:23.700 --> 01:21:29.400
No one can be certain. Even more inexplicable&nbsp;
is the entity at the center of all this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:21:29.400 --> 01:21:34.800
an unknown female presence capable of wreaking&nbsp;
frightening amounts of violence by turning&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:21:34.800 --> 01:21:40.080
victims’ own images against them. What is the&nbsp;
purpose of these funhouse mirror nightmares?&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:21:40.080 --> 01:21:45.240
Who is she, what is she, and what does she&nbsp;
want? Currently, the doubles have shown no&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:21:45.240 --> 01:21:50.640
interest in leaving the hotel except to attack&nbsp;
intruders, and thanks to that fact, as well as&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:21:50.640 --> 01:21:56.400
the reinforced perimeter outside, these copycats&nbsp;
have not appeared outside of the building itself.

01:21:56.400 --> 01:22:00.660
But what happens if they do escape,&nbsp;
or if the entity that controls them&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:22:00.660 --> 01:22:05.640
decides to make her home elsewhere? There&nbsp;
is no telling what could happen if this&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:22:05.640 --> 01:22:09.120
dark power is allowed to move&nbsp;
beyond its current containment.

01:22:09.120 --> 01:22:13.800
Are you prepared to fight a vision&nbsp;
of yourself, twisted almost beyond&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:22:13.800 --> 01:22:19.380
recognition, lunging after you with wide&nbsp;
bulbous eyes, unnaturally long arms,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:22:19.380 --> 01:22:25.680
and a distended jaw hanging down below its&nbsp;
neck? Better hope you never have to find out.

01:22:25.680 --> 01:22:31.080
In high school, the days tend to blend together&nbsp;
after a while. Math test, unrequited love,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:22:31.080 --> 01:22:36.960
annoying group project, stress, rinse, repeat.&nbsp;
Sometimes a big football game or a school dance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:22:36.960 --> 01:22:39.600
or maybe a fight in the hallway&nbsp;
breaks up the monotony a bit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:22:39.600 --> 01:22:43.320
but it’s normally pretty uneventful.
That’s always been fine by me. I’ve&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:22:43.320 --> 01:22:47.220
never tried to be a popular kid or the center&nbsp;
of attention, I prefer to keep my head down,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:22:47.220 --> 01:22:51.300
work stage crew for the school plays, and just&nbsp;
hang out with the same small group of friends&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:22:51.300 --> 01:22:54.900
I’ve known since we were little kids.
It was on one of these ordinary days,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:22:54.900 --> 01:23:00.300
in a long line of similarly ordinary days,&nbsp;
that something came to destroy the peaceful&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:23:00.300 --> 01:23:05.160
high school existence I’d gotten used to. As&nbsp;
I sat in history class, passing notes with&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:23:05.160 --> 01:23:09.960
my best friend Zach and ignoring a video about&nbsp;
the Civil War, I had no idea that I was about&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:23:09.960 --> 01:23:15.540
to live through the worst day of my life. And I&nbsp;
would be one of the lucky ones; I’d survive. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:23:15.540 --> 01:23:20.700
others…let’s just say they wouldn’t be so lucky.
I was just scribbling a response to Zach,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:23:20.700 --> 01:23:24.300
something about hanging out and playing&nbsp;
Xbox after school, when the PA system&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:23:24.300 --> 01:23:27.720
crackled to life. Our principal’s voice&nbsp;
cut through the droning narration about&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:23:27.720 --> 01:23:31.740
the Battle of Antietam as he spoke.
“Staff, this is a lockdown. Initiate&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:23:31.740 --> 01:23:35.280
your lockdown procedures immediately. If you&nbsp;
are a visitor outside the building, please&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:23:35.280 --> 01:23:39.960
leave the property immediately, and call 911.”
I assumed it was just another lockdown drill,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:23:39.960 --> 01:23:45.300
until I saw my teacher’s face. She looked pale,&nbsp;
her expression tight, like she was trying to hold&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:23:45.300 --> 01:23:49.500
it together for our benefit. I could see her hands&nbsp;
shaking as she reached to turn off the video,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:23:49.500 --> 01:23:55.320
and when I heard the tremor in her voice I knew&nbsp;
for sure: she was terrified. This was not a drill.&nbsp;

01:23:55.320 --> 01:23:58.680
As our teacher locked the door and we all&nbsp;
climbed under our desks to crouch in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:23:58.680 --> 01:24:03.000
dark and wait out the lockdown, I could hear&nbsp;
my classmates whispering feverishly. Everyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:24:03.000 --> 01:24:06.840
was trying to figure out what was going on.&nbsp;
Someone suggested a kid had brought a knife&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:24:06.840 --> 01:24:10.380
to school. Someone wondered aloud if a threat&nbsp;
had been called in to the principal’s office.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:24:10.380 --> 01:24:15.240
Zach cracked a dumb joke about a mutated frog&nbsp;
escaping from the biology lab, when suddenly&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:24:15.240 --> 01:24:20.220
a scream rang out, echoing down the hall.
Have you ever felt an entire room of people&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:24:20.220 --> 01:24:24.180
holding their breath at once? I have.
We listened for the sound of fighting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:24:24.180 --> 01:24:30.000
for gunshots, anything
...Nothing. And then another scream, louder,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:24:30.000 --> 01:24:35.400
closer, and longer than the last. It was a&nbsp;
scream of pure, unadulterated fear and pain&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:24:35.400 --> 01:24:39.780
that dissolved into a wet gurgle that made&nbsp;
my stomach turn. Zach and I shared a look,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:24:39.780 --> 01:24:43.800
one that said, “whatever is going on,&nbsp;
it’s like nothing we’ve ever seen before.”&nbsp;

01:24:43.800 --> 01:24:48.360
I could feel my chest tightening, and it was&nbsp;
getting harder to breathe. I tucked my head&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:24:48.360 --> 01:24:53.640
between my knees, holding onto the back of my head&nbsp;
and trying to take in deep gulps of air. The room&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:24:53.640 --> 01:24:58.320
felt as if it tilted on its side and I thought&nbsp;
I might pass out, when another sound brought me&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:24:58.320 --> 01:25:04.320
back to earth. It was coming from the back wall&nbsp;
of the classroom, by the chalkboard. The sound of&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:25:04.320 --> 01:25:09.540
liquid sloshing onto the floor, mixed with plaster&nbsp;
splintering apart and pieces clattering all over.&nbsp;

01:25:09.540 --> 01:25:12.600
I tried to get a better look, but the&nbsp;
room was dark and I didn’t want to leave&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:25:12.600 --> 01:25:17.460
the relative safety of my desk. If there&nbsp;
was someone, or something, coming into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:25:17.460 --> 01:25:20.820
room…I didn’t want it to see me.
Zach had a better angle than me,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:25:20.820 --> 01:25:24.480
I could see him craning his neck to get a&nbsp;
better look, when he clapped a hand over&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:25:24.480 --> 01:25:30.000
his mouth in shock. I heard him scream, muffled,&nbsp;
against his hand. What had he seen? What was it?&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:25:30.000 --> 01:25:33.360
Before I could even ask, my teacher’s cry&nbsp;
ripped through the darkness and the silence.&nbsp;

01:25:33.360 --> 01:25:38.760
“Get out! Get out!” She repeated over and over&nbsp;
again, and I could hear the raw desperation in her&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:25:38.760 --> 01:25:43.500
voice. It was like someone ushering passengers&nbsp;
off of the sinking Titanic, someone who knows&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:25:43.500 --> 01:25:47.700
there is no hope for them but hopes they can at&nbsp;
least save the children before it all goes down.&nbsp;

01:25:47.700 --> 01:25:54.060
“Run! For the love of God just run!” Her voice&nbsp;
broke, from fear, from pain, or both, and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:25:54.060 --> 01:25:58.500
sound was enough to get my legs working again. My&nbsp;
classmates had the same response, and we blindly&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:25:58.500 --> 01:26:02.340
rushed for the door, flipping over desks and&nbsp;
knocking chairs to the side as we scrambled for&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:26:02.340 --> 01:26:07.380
an exit. Zach grabbed my arm, and I held on tight,&nbsp;
afraid I would lose him in the chaos. Someone&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:26:07.380 --> 01:26:10.980
unlocked the door and we poured out into the hall.
Just as I made it out of the door, I couldn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:26:10.980 --> 01:26:16.200
help but turn back and look. Call it morbid&nbsp;
curiosity, call it instinct, call it stupidity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:26:16.200 --> 01:26:20.820
but I had to see what had happened. I turned&nbsp;
just in time to see a nightmare brought to life.&nbsp;

01:26:20.820 --> 01:26:28.380
The wall was melting, covered in something thick,&nbsp;
black, and putrid. The smell invaded my nostrils&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:26:28.380 --> 01:26:32.940
and I gagged on it. A wretched, grey arm had&nbsp;
its fingers wrapped around the teacher’s wrist,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:26:32.940 --> 01:26:37.320
skin peeling off to reveal muscle and bone.&nbsp;
It looked like it belonged to a corpse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:26:37.320 --> 01:26:42.000
but it gripped her with inhuman strength. She&nbsp;
was pulling with all her might, but I watched&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:26:42.000 --> 01:26:46.980
helplessly as the arm pulled her into the melted&nbsp;
wall like she weighed nothing, swallowing her body&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:26:46.980 --> 01:26:51.780
and her screams with it. And then she was gone.
Zach tugged on my arm, hard, yanking&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:26:51.780 --> 01:26:53.460
me into the hall.
“Come on man, run!”&nbsp;

01:26:53.460 --> 01:26:56.700
He hadn’t seen what I’d seen, or&nbsp;
he would have realized that running&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:26:56.700 --> 01:27:01.020
might not be enough. Whatever this thing&nbsp;
was, it didn’t play by any rules I knew.&nbsp;

01:27:01.020 --> 01:27:05.580
Running was all we had right now, though, so we&nbsp;
ran. I looked around for a weapon, something,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:27:05.580 --> 01:27:10.200
anything I could use to defend myself, but I&nbsp;
couldn’t see anything that would help. Instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:27:10.200 --> 01:27:14.340
all I saw was the destruction the intruder&nbsp;
had left in its wake. All around me,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:27:14.340 --> 01:27:19.800
the halls I walked through every day were falling&nbsp;
to pieces. They weren’t just damaged. They were&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:27:19.800 --> 01:27:24.840
coming apart at the seams. Lockers were warped&nbsp;
beyond recognition, walls completely dissolved,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:27:24.840 --> 01:27:28.800
sections of the floor reduced to&nbsp;
sizzling puddles of goo, and everywhere,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:27:28.800 --> 01:27:34.860
everything was covered in that same black slime.
It smelled worse than you can ever imagine. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:27:34.860 --> 01:27:39.780
smelled like the complete loss of hope, like&nbsp;
the point of no return. It smelled like death.&nbsp;

01:27:39.780 --> 01:27:43.860
We reached the end of the hall when I heard&nbsp;
something shifting behind us. I suddenly became&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:27:43.860 --> 01:27:49.440
aware that we were alone. The sounds of frantic&nbsp;
footsteps, hushed whispers, doors slamming shut&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:27:49.440 --> 01:27:54.600
and locking, had all quieted. Where was everyone?
I glanced over my shoulder, and saw one lone&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:27:54.600 --> 01:27:59.100
figure shambling down the hall toward us. It was&nbsp;
far away, and I could scarcely make it out in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:27:59.100 --> 01:28:04.620
darkness, but I could hear dripping, sizzling,&nbsp;
and the smell of decay grew stronger. That was&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:28:04.620 --> 01:28:09.960
not a classmate or a teacher. Whatever it was, it&nbsp;
was taking people away, or killing them, I didn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:28:09.960 --> 01:28:14.640
know exactly what. But whatever it was doing&nbsp;
to everyone, Zach and I were next on its list.&nbsp;

01:28:14.640 --> 01:28:20.160
The scariest part was how slowly it moved. Maybe&nbsp;
its legs were too rotten to move any faster,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:28:20.160 --> 01:28:26.040
joints disintegrating into useless mush, but&nbsp;
it seemed more deliberate than that. To me,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:28:26.040 --> 01:28:31.200
in my panic-clouded mind, it seemed that it&nbsp;
was taking its time. It didn’t need to rush,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:28:31.200 --> 01:28:35.460
it knew that, when it wanted to catch&nbsp;
its prey, it would. I couldn’t suppress&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:28:35.460 --> 01:28:39.420
the sick feeling in my stomach this time,&nbsp;
I keeled over and vomited onto the floor.&nbsp;

01:28:39.420 --> 01:28:42.960
When I looked up, Zach was beckoning to me&nbsp;
from just inside the doors to the auditorium.&nbsp;

01:28:42.960 --> 01:28:45.480
“Come on! In here!”
He could have left me&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:28:45.480 --> 01:28:50.640
behind for the intruder to take, tried to save&nbsp;
himself, and sacrifice the slow friend frozen in&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:28:50.640 --> 01:28:55.440
place with terror, but here he was looking out&nbsp;
for me again. Even in this horrible situation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:28:55.440 --> 01:28:59.880
I felt a surge of gratitude. I booked it&nbsp;
across the floor, forgetting for a moment&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:28:59.880 --> 01:29:04.320
about the shuffling corpse making its way toward&nbsp;
us, and joined my best friend in the auditorium.&nbsp;

01:29:04.320 --> 01:29:08.880
It was eerie in the dark, the curtain&nbsp;
soaking up and dampening sounds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:29:08.880 --> 01:29:13.320
barely any light illuminating the normally&nbsp;
cheerful props and backdrops left from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:29:13.320 --> 01:29:18.960
recent production of Alice in Wonderland. A once&nbsp;
friendly place felt twisted, like a mockery of&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:29:18.960 --> 01:29:23.700
Wonderland with a monster stalking outside&nbsp;
and waiting to pounce. We sat on the stage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:29:23.700 --> 01:29:28.620
listening to the sound of our labored breathing.&nbsp;
The air felt heavy, but I welcomed the smell of&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:29:28.620 --> 01:29:32.160
paint and dust over the nauseating stench&nbsp;
that permeated the rest of the school.&nbsp;

01:29:34.080 --> 01:29:39.060
“Are we the only ones left?” Zach whispered,&nbsp;
breaking the silence. He was the first one to say&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:29:39.060 --> 01:29:45.180
what we were both thinking, what we both feared.
“No.” I said with false confidence. “I think some&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:29:45.180 --> 01:29:50.220
of them got out, before…” I couldn’t finish the&nbsp;
sentence. “Somebody had to get out. It can’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:29:50.220 --> 01:29:54.960
just be us.” I leaned my head against a giant&nbsp;
papier-mache toadstool, glad it was too dark for&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:29:54.960 --> 01:29:59.100
Zach to see the tears filling my eyes.
“What was that thing?” He asked.&nbsp;

01:29:59.100 --> 01:30:02.640
“Did you see it?” I sat up straighter.&nbsp;
I thought I was the only one who’d&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:30:02.640 --> 01:30:08.700
gotten a look at the thing, however fleeting.
“No. But I heard it. And…smelled it.” He coughed.&nbsp;

01:30:08.700 --> 01:30:13.800
It took me a while to answer his question.&nbsp;
Eventually, I found the word. “It’s evil.”&nbsp;

01:30:13.800 --> 01:30:20.040
We sat in silence for a long while after that. I&nbsp;
don’t know exactly how long. Moments like that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:30:20.040 --> 01:30:25.740
where at any second you could be lost forever,&nbsp;
time stretches out into something unrecognizable.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:30:25.740 --> 01:30:30.540
I was starting to think, foolishly, that we&nbsp;
might be in the clear, when I heard a strange&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:30:30.540 --> 01:30:36.660
sound. It was a creaking, like footsteps on&nbsp;
an old wooden floor. I looked around for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:30:36.660 --> 01:30:43.360
source of the noise, but I couldn’t see anything.
It sounded close, impossibly close. Creak. Creak.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:30:44.340 --> 01:30:48.540
One step then another. Where was that&nbsp;
coming from? There was no wood floor in&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:30:48.540 --> 01:30:51.360
the hall, nothing above us.
By the time I understood,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:30:51.360 --> 01:30:57.420
it was too late. The top of a head, slimy, clammy&nbsp;
and grey, with tufts of limp white hair clinging&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:30:57.420 --> 01:31:02.640
to the soft flesh began to emerge from the&nbsp;
stage where we sat. Eyes, hollow and dead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:31:02.640 --> 01:31:07.560
but somehow alert and searching for us,&nbsp;
came next, followed by a gaping wound where&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:31:07.560 --> 01:31:13.380
a nose should be, and a wide, toothless grin.
It looked almost like a person, but it was wrong.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:31:13.380 --> 01:31:19.140
Just wrong. Every cell in my body rejected it,&nbsp;
screaming at me with thousands of years of animal&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:31:19.140 --> 01:31:23.340
instinct that I had to run. I grabbed Zach’s&nbsp;
arm and yanked, but he didn’t come with me.&nbsp;

01:31:23.340 --> 01:31:28.920
I turned to look, and my heart jumped into my&nbsp;
throat. It had him. Its bony fingers had a hold&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:31:28.920 --> 01:31:34.260
on his legs, and he was already halfway gone,&nbsp;
pulled into a slick black puddle in the stage.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:31:34.260 --> 01:31:39.660
His face was damp with tears, as the reality&nbsp;
of his fate set in. He grabbed my hand in his,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:31:39.660 --> 01:31:44.400
and squeezed. “Run.” Was all he could get out,&nbsp;
before the old man pulled him out of sight.&nbsp;

01:31:44.400 --> 01:31:49.140
So I obeyed my best friend’s wish.&nbsp;
I ran, and I hid in the prop closet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:31:49.140 --> 01:31:53.580
hand over my mouth to stifle my breathing.&nbsp;
Suddenly, there was a loud bang, and I heard&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:31:53.580 --> 01:31:58.590
voices yelling. Something that sounded like a&nbsp;
gunshot. A blast of bright light. Then, a voice,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:31:58.590 --> 01:32:02.880
male and official-sounding, called out: “Is anyone&nbsp;
in here? You can come out, we’re with the police.”&nbsp;

01:32:02.880 --> 01:32:07.440
I opened the closet door and peered out, to see&nbsp;
people in hazmat suits wielding bizarre weapons&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:32:07.440 --> 01:32:11.520
and carrying devices I’d never seen before.
The man who had spoken approached me,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:32:11.520 --> 01:32:16.980
took my hand, and asked me if I’d seen anything. I&nbsp;
got the strong sense that I should definitely not&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:32:16.980 --> 01:32:22.800
tell him what I’d seen. “No, sir,” I said.
He nodded. Whether he believed me or not,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:32:22.800 --> 01:32:27.240
he knew I wouldn’t say anything more.
“Gas leak.” He said. “It destroyed large&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:32:27.240 --> 01:32:29.760
parts of the building. Highly dangerous.&nbsp;
We need to get you out of here.”&nbsp;

01:32:29.760 --> 01:32:34.920
They took me home and I hugged my parents&nbsp;
tighter than I ever had before. That night,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:32:34.920 --> 01:32:39.180
the news covered the tragedy at my school.&nbsp;
The “gas leak” had taken dozens of lives&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:32:39.180 --> 01:32:43.200
before the authorities had gotten there.
Everyone else can accept that story all&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:32:43.200 --> 01:32:48.720
they want. I know the truth. I see it when&nbsp;
I close my eyes, imagine it standing over&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:32:48.720 --> 01:32:54.360
me when I wake up in the dead of night.&nbsp;
Those hollow eyes, that horrible smile,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:32:54.360 --> 01:33:02.160
the stench of death and rot. It looked right&nbsp;
at me. It saw me. It wanted…I can’t let myself&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:33:02.160 --> 01:33:05.640
think about what it wanted.
I don’t know exactly what I saw,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:33:05.640 --> 01:33:11.220
but I know a few things for certain: There was&nbsp;
no gas leak. Zach and the rest of the people&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:33:11.220 --> 01:33:16.440
it took are gone. And, if that monster&nbsp;
ever escapes…it’s coming after me next.

01:33:16.440 --> 01:33:22.380
Throwing indestructible lizards into vats
of acid, hunting strange chicken men through

01:33:22.380 --> 01:33:27.780
forests in Ireland, arguing in Latin with
a man wearing a haunted Roman Centurion’s

01:33:27.780 --> 01:33:28.140
helmet.

01:33:28.140 --> 01:33:33.720
When you join the SCP Foundation, you might
be expecting high-octane drama all the time.

01:33:33.720 --> 01:33:38.580
Especially with the name Street Sweepers,
you’d expect this Mobile Task Force to be

01:33:38.580 --> 01:33:41.520
neck deep in some real action-packed street
racing.

01:33:41.520 --> 01:33:47.340
Maybe you wouldn’t think that they’d be
tasked with driving all day every day in four-hour

01:33:47.340 --> 01:33:51.900
shifts, tailing a semi-truck, all over Birmingham,
Alabama.

01:33:51.900 --> 01:33:56.880
But as Agent Moore and his colleague pulled
into the layby behind the truck, neither of

01:33:56.880 --> 01:33:59.400
them were ready for what they were about to
witness…

01:33:59.400 --> 01:34:00.570
*

01:34:00.570 --> 01:34:05.100
SCP-2590 was first discovered by the Foundation
at a routine traffic stop.

01:34:05.100 --> 01:34:10.080
Investigating a totally different anomaly
in the Birmingham area, Agents Peters and

01:34:10.080 --> 01:34:13.020
Smith had been posing as local police officers.

01:34:13.020 --> 01:34:17.820
The Foundation had been trying to track down
an artifact that was supposedly being smuggled

01:34:17.820 --> 01:34:21.480
across the US in the back of a non-descript
station wagon.

01:34:21.480 --> 01:34:27.120
Peters and Smith had been allocated a pair
of beat-up old police cruisers which they’d

01:34:27.120 --> 01:34:31.320
parked across the dirt road, fully blocking
any traffic from coming through.

01:34:31.320 --> 01:34:36.510
It was several hours into their shift, when
the incident occurred, just at the point that

01:34:36.510 --> 01:34:38.160
they were starting to lose focus.

01:34:38.160 --> 01:34:41.400
Taking a look through the&nbsp;
suitcases and memorabilia&nbsp;

01:34:41.400 --> 01:34:43.740
from a family’s trip to Disney World, Peters

01:34:43.740 --> 01:34:47.820
had taken way too long to hear the noise of
the engine swelling behind him.

01:34:47.820 --> 01:34:52.560
He spun around to see the hulking shape of
the semi-truck barreling straight towards

01:34:52.560 --> 01:34:55.440
him, Agent Smith, and a family of five.

01:34:55.440 --> 01:35:00.000
With only two seconds to react, he yelled
out at the top of his lungs and dived out

01:35:00.000 --> 01:35:04.440
of the way, leaving the trunk of the car wide
open with five screams emerging from inside.

01:35:04.440 --> 01:35:09.360
Smith, who had been sitting in one of the
cruisers, only just managed to get out before

01:35:09.360 --> 01:35:10.680
the semi made contact.

01:35:10.680 --> 01:35:13.680
Eyes closed, Agent Peters&nbsp;
waited for the inevitable&nbsp;

01:35:13.680 --> 01:35:16.020
sound of screaming rubber, the bang of metal

01:35:16.020 --> 01:35:19.080
on metal, and the shower of glass on asphalt.

01:35:19.080 --> 01:35:20.220
But it never came.

01:35:20.220 --> 01:35:25.140
When he opened his eyes, the station wagon
was still parked up in front of them, the

01:35:25.140 --> 01:35:29.880
two police cruisers still blocking the road,
and all of the Disney merch still piled high

01:35:29.880 --> 01:35:30.720
in the trunk.

01:35:30.720 --> 01:35:36.360
The semi was driving off along the road on
the other side of their blockade, not a scratch

01:35:36.360 --> 01:35:36.960
on it.

01:35:36.960 --> 01:35:41.460
Without a moment's hesitation, Agent Smith,
who had kept his eyes open and witnessed the

01:35:41.460 --> 01:35:43.140
whole thing, leaped into action.

01:35:43.140 --> 01:35:48.180
He ordered his partner, still lying confused
in the dirt, to administer Class-A amnestics

01:35:48.180 --> 01:35:50.280
to the family and call in for backup.

01:35:50.280 --> 01:35:55.440
Agent Smith himself jammed his keys into the
ignition, twisted them so hard he almost bent

01:35:55.440 --> 01:35:57.960
the metal, and took off after the vehicle.

01:35:57.960 --> 01:36:03.360
What Agents Smith and Peters had just witnessed
was the very first Foundation exposure to

01:36:03.360 --> 01:36:07.500
SCP-2590, fondly nicknamed Trailer Trash.

01:36:07.500 --> 01:36:12.960
As Smith pulled up alongside the vehicle and
studied it for the first time, he made a note

01:36:12.960 --> 01:36:17.940
of its initial appearance over the radio,
an appearance which remains unchanged years

01:36:17.940 --> 01:36:18.240
later.

01:36:18.240 --> 01:36:23.880
The badges on the vehicle claim that it is
an International ProStar DayCab semi-trailer

01:36:23.880 --> 01:36:26.280
truck, complete with an unmarked trailer.

01:36:26.280 --> 01:36:31.380
As the Agent flicked on his lights and indicated
that the vehicle should pull over, he noted

01:36:31.380 --> 01:36:35.400
that it didn’t have any license plates on
it, either front or rear.

01:36:35.400 --> 01:36:40.080
He leaned forward in his seat, trying to peer
into the cab to make out the driver, but in

01:36:40.080 --> 01:36:43.620
the Alabama sun, the man just looked like
a shadowy figure.

01:36:43.620 --> 01:36:46.980
They drove side by side along the road for
almost a mile.

01:36:46.980 --> 01:36:52.980
The truck made no signs of pulling over despite
Agent Smith’s continued insistence and repeated

01:36:52.980 --> 01:36:57.780
flashes of the cop lights, but it also didn’t
attempt to pull away either.

01:36:57.780 --> 01:37:02.280
It just continued to drive a few miles per
hour below the speed limit.

01:37:02.280 --> 01:37:05.460
The driver didn’t seem to look across at
him once.

01:37:05.460 --> 01:37:09.720
Having discussed it with Foundation staff,
they decided that it was best not to draw

01:37:09.720 --> 01:37:11.100
attention to the situation.

01:37:11.100 --> 01:37:16.740
They had no idea whether this SCP was hostile
or posed any threat to civilian life, but

01:37:16.740 --> 01:37:20.700
having blue and red lights flashing at it
appeared to be doing little to change the

01:37:20.700 --> 01:37:21.180
situation.

01:37:21.180 --> 01:37:26.940
Instead, he switched off the sirens and pulled
in behind the truck, tailing it around Birmingham

01:37:26.940 --> 01:37:30.720
as the Foundation readied further agents to
respond to the situation.

01:37:30.720 --> 01:37:33.480
For almost an hour, nothing of note happened.

01:37:33.480 --> 01:37:37.380
Agent Smith drove behind the trailer, watching
it like a hawk.

01:37:37.380 --> 01:37:42.960
He observed that it obeyed every traffic law
to a T. It never broke the speed limit, never

01:37:42.960 --> 01:37:46.680
cut anyone off, and left room for other vehicles
to merge.

01:37:46.680 --> 01:37:51.000
If hadn’t seen it drive straight through
a roadblock as if it wasn’t there, he would

01:37:51.000 --> 01:37:52.920
never have suspected a thing.

01:37:52.920 --> 01:37:55.620
But then the truck turned its turn signal
on.

01:37:55.620 --> 01:38:00.420
They had just come off the highway and merged
onto a quiet side street, just as the sun

01:38:00.420 --> 01:38:02.100
was starting to hang low in the sky.

01:38:02.640 --> 01:38:07.740
The truck crept across to the side of the
road, squeezing its brakes gently, and stopped.

01:38:07.740 --> 01:38:12.720
Agent Smith matched the action the whole way,
pulling up about twenty feet behind the trailer.

01:38:12.720 --> 01:38:17.400
In constant radio communication, he kicked
open his door and stepped out into the evening

01:38:17.400 --> 01:38:17.820
air.

01:38:17.820 --> 01:38:22.740
Foundation personnel advised that he keep
a hand on his gun at all times and approach

01:38:22.740 --> 01:38:23.520
with caution.

01:38:23.520 --> 01:38:26.100
He didn’t really need them to tell him that.

01:38:26.100 --> 01:38:28.680
Smith called out for the driver to step out
of the cab.

01:38:28.680 --> 01:38:29.880
No response.

01:38:29.880 --> 01:38:33.480
The truck just sat there with its hazards
on, engine off.

01:38:33.480 --> 01:38:39.360
After a moment, there was a clunk, and the
trailer door started to slowly open, all by

01:38:39.360 --> 01:38:39.780
itself.

01:38:39.780 --> 01:38:43.620
Agent Smith called in backup, but they were
still several minutes out.

01:38:43.620 --> 01:38:48.900
Instead, he ran back to the car, gun raised,
and waited to see what was inside as the door

01:38:48.900 --> 01:38:50.340
slowly opened to reveal…

01:38:50.340 --> 01:38:51.060
Nothing.

01:38:51.060 --> 01:38:52.740
No, not quite nothing.

01:38:52.740 --> 01:38:57.180
There was something small on the floor of
the trailer, right in the center, as if it

01:38:57.180 --> 01:38:59.880
hadn’t been moved around at all by the vehicle’s
motion.

01:38:59.880 --> 01:39:00.840
It was red.

01:39:00.840 --> 01:39:02.580
A kind of elongated cuboid.

01:39:03.120 --> 01:39:08.040
He reported it all to the Foundation over
his radio, then paused when he recognized

01:39:08.040 --> 01:39:08.700
what it was.

01:39:08.700 --> 01:39:10.680
A Kit Kat candy bar.

01:39:10.680 --> 01:39:14.760
Or, to be more specific, a Kit Kat Chunky.

01:39:14.760 --> 01:39:17.040
What happened after this point was hazy.

01:39:17.040 --> 01:39:21.600
Agent Smith was found on the roadside just
twenty minutes later, confused about what

01:39:21.600 --> 01:39:21.960
had happened.

01:39:21.960 --> 01:39:24.180
The truck was nowhere in sight.

01:39:24.180 --> 01:39:28.740
However, a security camera from a convenience
store just up the street happened to capture

01:39:28.740 --> 01:39:29.460
the interaction.

01:39:29.460 --> 01:39:34.200
In the footage, you see Agent Smith approaching
the trailer with his gun raised, looking at

01:39:34.200 --> 01:39:34.800
the Kit Kat.

01:39:34.800 --> 01:39:39.960
He tries to enter the trailer but is unable
to, so approaches the driver’s side door.

01:39:39.960 --> 01:39:44.640
While talking to the shadowy figure in the
cab, he drops his gun and stands motionless,

01:39:44.640 --> 01:39:50.280
a confused and sleepy expression on his face,
until the trailer door closes and the SCP

01:39:50.280 --> 01:39:50.940
drives away.

01:39:50.940 --> 01:39:57.900
Contact was reestablished with SCP-2590 soon
after and has been maintained almost uninterrupted

01:39:57.900 --> 01:39:58.620
ever since.

01:39:58.620 --> 01:40:04.020
The findings made on that initial encounter
seem to hold true across further examination.

01:40:04.020 --> 01:40:06.600
Personnel has reached out&nbsp;
to Navistar International,&nbsp;

01:40:06.600 --> 01:40:09.720
the company that supposedly manufactures this

01:40:09.720 --> 01:40:14.520
model of semi-truck, but there appear to be
no records of its creation or shipment to

01:40:14.520 --> 01:40:15.000
the US.

01:40:15.000 --> 01:40:21.300
In fact, no documentation at all can be attributed
to the truck or any components on it.

01:40:21.300 --> 01:40:26.520
The driver in the front cab is a humanoid
figure who is perpetually shrouded in shadow,

01:40:26.520 --> 01:40:29.520
designated SCP-2590-1.

01:40:29.520 --> 01:40:34.500
Attempts to reveal the driver’s features
have proven ineffective, as even powerful

01:40:34.500 --> 01:40:39.060
spotlights do not shed enough light into the
cab to render the driver visible.

01:40:39.060 --> 01:40:44.640
Quite what this driver’s role is in the
operation of SCP-2590 is unknown.

01:40:44.640 --> 01:40:51.480
SCP-2590-1 appears to have some proximity-based
amnestic qualities, as anyone approaching

01:40:51.480 --> 01:40:56.880
it on foot has reported memory loss and confusion
soon after, just like Agent Smith.

01:40:56.880 --> 01:41:02.520
As also discovered by the two agents and their
roadblock, containment of this SCP is simply

01:41:02.520 --> 01:41:03.480
not possible.

01:41:03.480 --> 01:41:08.580
While the majority of the time, the SCP is
corporeal, it possesses the ability to pass

01:41:08.580 --> 01:41:10.260
through solid objects at will.

01:41:10.260 --> 01:41:15.660
All attempted roadblocks have resulted in
the same thing happening, the SCP will just

01:41:15.660 --> 01:41:18.720
phase right on through them as if nothing
was there.

01:41:18.720 --> 01:41:23.580
Since it cannot be contained in the usual
way, a different operation has been set up

01:41:23.580 --> 01:41:28.500
to monitor the truck’s activities which
so far have proven to be apparently harmless

01:41:28.500 --> 01:41:29.760
to the civilian population.

01:41:29.760 --> 01:41:35.700
Mobile Task Force Gamma 133, also known as
the street sweepers, has been established

01:41:35.700 --> 01:41:39.480
to follow this SCP around Birmingham at all
times.

01:41:39.480 --> 01:41:44.820
They operate in four-hour shifts, with two
agents in unmarked vehicles sticking close

01:41:44.820 --> 01:41:46.680
behind the trailer at all times.

01:41:46.680 --> 01:41:51.660
The Foundation was able to fit a tracking
device onto it as well, providing researchers

01:41:51.660 --> 01:41:55.260
with continuous location data for where they
can find the vehicle.

01:41:55.260 --> 01:42:01.200
At seemingly random times, supposedly determined
by the SCP itself, it pulls over somewhere

01:42:01.200 --> 01:42:03.600
quiet and opens the door to its trailer.

01:42:03.600 --> 01:42:07.860
The door will remain open for 60 seconds,
and then close again.

01:42:07.860 --> 01:42:12.840
Any attempts to enter the trailer have been
blocked by some kind of invisible barrier,

01:42:12.840 --> 01:42:15.840
seemingly impenetrable to most approaches.

01:42:15.840 --> 01:42:21.000
More violent and destructive methods of entry
cannot be authorized for testing, due to the

01:42:21.000 --> 01:42:23.700
heavy civilian population in the surrounding
area.

01:42:23.700 --> 01:42:27.720
Every time the doors open, there is something
different in the trailer.

01:42:27.720 --> 01:42:32.820
Researchers are trying to ascertain some kind
of pattern or messaging behind most of the

01:42:32.820 --> 01:42:34.980
objects, but many seem to be random.

01:42:34.980 --> 01:42:40.320
The current list of things that have appeared
in the back of SCP-2590 include an iPhone

01:42:40.320 --> 01:42:45.780
3G, a red apple, and a lit lightbulb without
any visible form of power supply.

01:42:45.780 --> 01:42:51.300
Most notable about the objects in the trailer
is that often they appear to be human beings,

01:42:51.300 --> 01:42:55.920
as happened on the night that Agent Moore
was on duty in the Street Sweepers.

01:42:55.920 --> 01:42:56.220
*

01:42:56.220 --> 01:43:01.080
The Agents pulled in behind the truck as per
usual when it slowed to a stop beside the

01:43:01.080 --> 01:43:01.260
highway.

01:43:01.260 --> 01:43:06.060
Agent Moore got out of the vehicle second,
unenthused about the monotony of the task

01:43:06.060 --> 01:43:07.260
that he had been assigned.

01:43:07.260 --> 01:43:12.120
Expecting to see a cardboard box or a chapstick
when the trailer door opened, he was left

01:43:12.120 --> 01:43:15.360
shocked when he came face to face with himself.

01:43:15.360 --> 01:43:21.060
Few people can say that they have seen themselves
in real life, most of them have been administered

01:43:21.060 --> 01:43:25.920
with various amnestics to make them forget,
but Agent Moore went on to report how bizarre

01:43:25.920 --> 01:43:27.240
of an experience it was.

01:43:27.240 --> 01:43:32.220
He claimed that it was utterly unlike looking
in a mirror where your reflection is flipped

01:43:32.220 --> 01:43:33.540
and follows your every move.

01:43:33.540 --> 01:43:39.300
Seeing yourself standing in three dimensions,
moving independently and evidently in a great

01:43:39.300 --> 01:43:42.900
deal of distress, is an experience that few
would envy.

01:43:42.900 --> 01:43:47.640
Any time a human being materializes in the
trailer, they appear to be in a great deal

01:43:47.640 --> 01:43:51.240
of distress as they attempt to escape through
the invisible barrier.

01:43:51.240 --> 01:43:56.460
Agent Moore and his partner Agent Hall could
do nothing but stand and watch in confusion

01:43:56.460 --> 01:44:02.280
as the copy of him attempted to free himself
before, after the usual 60 seconds, the trailer

01:44:02.280 --> 01:44:04.920
door closed, and the vehicle pulled away again.

01:44:04.920 --> 01:44:09.780
Several instances have occurred of duplicate
humans appearing in the trailer, but each

01:44:09.780 --> 01:44:14.220
time the ‘original’ person seems to have
had no knowledge of this taking place, and

01:44:14.220 --> 01:44:16.200
nothing out of the ordinary happens to them.

01:44:16.200 --> 01:44:21.420
However, there appears to be some small pattern
demonstrating the SCP has an awareness of

01:44:21.420 --> 01:44:26.940
the Foundation as it has also duplicated Agent
Inglis’s sister, who has no connection to

01:44:26.940 --> 01:44:28.200
this SCP at all.

01:44:28.200 --> 01:44:33.780
Incident 16 was the most distressing of all,
as a large slab of metal appeared in the back

01:44:33.780 --> 01:44:37.320
of the trailer with the SCP Foundation logo
painted across it.

01:44:37.320 --> 01:44:42.300
Agents Inglis and Shultz were on duty at the
time and observed copious amounts of blood

01:44:42.300 --> 01:44:43.860
flowing out of the metal slab.

01:44:43.860 --> 01:44:48.540
Before long, the blood filled the back of
the trailer, pushing up against the invisible

01:44:48.540 --> 01:44:49.020
barrier.

01:44:49.020 --> 01:44:55.080
All of a sudden, 52 seconds into the encounter,
the barrier vanished, and a cascade of blood

01:44:55.080 --> 01:45:01.080
with the slab inside were launched out at
the two agents at a speed of over 190 kilometers

01:45:01.080 --> 01:45:03.600
an hour, killing them both instantly.

01:45:03.600 --> 01:45:08.820
Since this incident, SCP-2590 has been treated
with greater caution.

01:45:08.820 --> 01:45:13.500
The most mysterious thing to have come from
researching this truck came on December 4th,

01:45:13.500 --> 01:45:18.660
2011, when for the first time, the truck’s
tracking beacon stopped working.

01:45:18.660 --> 01:45:23.520
It had been seen pulling into an abandoned
warehouse and so a team of Street Sweepers

01:45:23.520 --> 01:45:25.740
was immediately dispatched to investigate.

01:45:25.740 --> 01:45:30.000
When they arrived, they found the vehicle
moving through the warehouse at a slow crawl.

01:45:30.000 --> 01:45:34.980
Choosing to pursue on foot and leaving a pair
of agents at the entrance, they followed the

01:45:34.980 --> 01:45:40.320
SCP through the facility until it came to
what agents described as a ‘service tunnel

01:45:40.320 --> 01:45:41.820
or sewer of some sort’.

01:45:41.820 --> 01:45:46.800
Putting headlamps on, they followed the truck
down into the tunnel, maintaining radio contact

01:45:46.800 --> 01:45:47.580
throughout.

01:45:47.580 --> 01:45:52.440
As they reported the direction they were traveling
and the distance, it quickly became apparent

01:45:52.440 --> 01:45:55.800
to Foundation personnel that this was no ordinary
tunnel.

01:45:55.800 --> 01:46:01.380
The warehouse was positioned overlooking a
cliff, and so the geography was not physically

01:46:01.380 --> 01:46:01.980
possible.

01:46:01.980 --> 01:46:06.600
As the Street Sweepers descended further into
the tunnel, they noted that there were increased

01:46:06.600 --> 01:46:08.040
levels of carbon monoxide.

01:46:08.040 --> 01:46:13.080
Radio contact started to dip in and out, losing
signal as they went further downhill.

01:46:13.080 --> 01:46:18.180
Just at the edge of their signal with the
Foundation, the truck stopped and opened its

01:46:18.180 --> 01:46:18.720
trailer door.

01:46:18.720 --> 01:46:24.000
Inside was just a single piece of parchment
with the words ‘I'm just delivering a message’

01:46:24.000 --> 01:46:24.900
written on it.

01:46:24.900 --> 01:46:29.700
After the usual 60 seconds, the trailer door
closed, and the truck continued.

01:46:29.700 --> 01:46:34.380
After they had passed the kilometer mark,
the radio signal worsened quickly, and after

01:46:34.380 --> 01:46:38.220
a couple of scrambled messages, the team down
there were not heard from again.

01:46:38.220 --> 01:46:43.200
The channel stayed open for another 6 hours
before the Foundation made the decision to

01:46:43.200 --> 01:46:45.360
announce the agents missing in action.

01:46:45.360 --> 01:46:51.540
In March 2015, over three years later, a radio
signal came into contact with the Foundation

01:46:51.540 --> 01:46:53.460
again from Birmingham, Alabama.

01:46:53.460 --> 01:46:57.360
It was from the headset of the squad leader
who had gone into the tunnel.

01:46:57.360 --> 01:47:02.460
Initially confused as to who had gained access
to the comms channel, the Foundation demanded

01:47:02.460 --> 01:47:04.800
that the agent state his full name and rank.

01:47:04.800 --> 01:47:09.840
The agent, himself confused, obliged, questioning
why they were so suspicious.

01:47:09.840 --> 01:47:13.440
He and his team claimed to have only lost
contact for about fifteen minutes.

01:47:13.440 --> 01:47:18.420
They had followed the SCP a little further
until carbon monoxide levels had risen too

01:47:18.420 --> 01:47:22.380
high to continue, at which point they’d
had to watched the truck disappearing into

01:47:22.380 --> 01:47:24.780
the distance as they walked back to the surface.

01:47:24.780 --> 01:47:30.360
All agents have undergone extensive psychological
rehabilitation to settle them back into society,

01:47:30.360 --> 01:47:32.820
as well as classes to fill them in on things&nbsp;

01:47:32.820 --> 01:47:35.400
like the London Olympics,&nbsp;
the Ice Bucket Challenge,

01:47:35.400 --> 01:47:37.320
and Gangnam style.

01:47:37.320 --> 01:47:44.940
As for SCP-2590, it is back out on the roads,
roaming around Birmingham, Alabama continuously.

01:47:44.940 --> 01:47:50.640
Never stopping for fuel, always obeying the
rules of the road, occasionally opening its

01:47:50.640 --> 01:47:54.240
trailer doors to reveal new and bizarre findings…

01:47:54.240 --> 01:48:00.060
A D-Class drag-races through the testing zone,
screaming at the top of his lungs and doing

01:48:00.060 --> 01:48:00.780
donuts.

01:48:00.780 --> 01:48:05.760
A mime who is also in the testing chamber
stares with disapproval, tapping his foot

01:48:05.760 --> 01:48:06.720
impatiently.

01:48:06.720 --> 01:48:09.240
Did we mention that the car is made of spiders?

01:48:09.240 --> 01:48:11.580
Yeah, this is gonna be a weird one, folks.

01:48:11.580 --> 01:48:16.080
Stay tuned for one of the craziest SCP stories
you’ve ever heard…

01:48:16.080 --> 01:48:19.620
Emily had always dreamed of taking a trip
to Paris.

01:48:19.620 --> 01:48:23.820
When the opportunity actually came to visit
the city, she was overjoyed.

01:48:23.820 --> 01:48:29.220
She spent her time exploring art museums,
tasting the bread and cheese, and walking

01:48:29.220 --> 01:48:32.160
through the city streets, taking in the sights.

01:48:32.160 --> 01:48:35.640
One of her favorite things about Paris was
all of the street performers.

01:48:35.640 --> 01:48:41.520
As she walked, nibbling on a pain au chocolat,
she delighted in the antics of jugglers, tossing

01:48:41.520 --> 01:48:43.200
colorful balls into the air.

01:48:43.200 --> 01:48:49.500
She gasped at the feats of athleticism and
grace demonstrated by acrobats and contortionists.

01:48:49.500 --> 01:48:54.600
She giggled at the absurd shows put on by
puppeteers, and dabbed tears from her eyes

01:48:54.600 --> 01:48:58.140
at the sound of beautiful songs played and
sung by musicians.

01:48:58.140 --> 01:49:00.540
It became part of her daily routine.

01:49:00.540 --> 01:49:05.580
One night, as Emily was walking back to her
hostel after a long, languid dinner, she found

01:49:05.580 --> 01:49:08.640
herself walking down a street she had not
encountered before.

01:49:08.640 --> 01:49:10.920
There was no one around except for her.

01:49:10.920 --> 01:49:16.680
It was a lovely moment of peace, but it also
struck her as a little bit eerie, and she

01:49:16.680 --> 01:49:18.660
wished for the familiar throngs of people.

01:49:18.660 --> 01:49:23.640
Up ahead, she spotted the silhouette of another
person, and let out a sigh of relief.

01:49:23.640 --> 01:49:28.800
As she got closer, she could make out the
black and white striped shirt, the suspenders,

01:49:28.800 --> 01:49:33.780
the black beret, the white face makeup, rouged
cheeks, and red lips.

01:49:33.780 --> 01:49:34.860
A mime!

01:49:34.860 --> 01:49:37.740
A real, classic French mime!

01:49:37.740 --> 01:49:39.360
She couldn't believe her luck.

01:49:39.360 --> 01:49:43.320
When he spotted Emily approaching, the mime
began to start a performance.

01:49:43.320 --> 01:49:46.320
He began with a classic: the invisible box.

01:49:46.320 --> 01:49:51.600
He felt around the walls of the invisible
box, looking out with exaggerated wide eyes

01:49:51.600 --> 01:49:52.680
and an open mouth.

01:49:52.680 --> 01:49:57.600
Emily clapped, and reached into her bag for
a little bit of money she could use to tip

01:49:57.600 --> 01:49:57.780
him.

01:49:57.780 --> 01:50:00.900
After all, he was putting on a performance
just for her.

01:50:00.900 --> 01:50:02.040
He deserved it!

01:50:02.040 --> 01:50:05.880
She walked closer to the mime, looking for
a place to put her tip.

01:50:05.880 --> 01:50:10.500
She didn't see one, so she held up her hand,
offering the money directly to the mime.

01:50:10.500 --> 01:50:15.540
As he took notice of how close she was getting,
the mime began shaking his head vigorously,

01:50:15.540 --> 01:50:17.820
eyes wide and insistent.

01:50:17.820 --> 01:50:22.500
She didn't understand that he was trying to
warn her, until it was too late.

01:50:22.500 --> 01:50:27.720
Dozens and dozens of spiders began to crawl
over the mime's face, out from inside of his

01:50:27.720 --> 01:50:32.880
clothes, from his shoes, pouring over the
street and crawling up onto Emily.

01:50:32.880 --> 01:50:37.800
She tried to brush them off, she tried to
run away, but no matter how hard she tried,

01:50:37.800 --> 01:50:40.200
the spiders just kept coming.

01:50:40.200 --> 01:50:42.480
All she could do was scream.

01:50:42.480 --> 01:50:47.940
In an attempt to experience a little bit of
live performance, Emily unwittingly came across

01:50:47.940 --> 01:50:50.640
SCP-3247.

01:50:50.640 --> 01:50:56.880
SCP-3247 is a humanoid entity standing at
approximately 1.7 meters in height.

01:50:56.880 --> 01:51:02.820
It wears a striped shirt and suspenders similar
to the garb of a stereotypical French mime,

01:51:02.820 --> 01:51:08.160
as well as what appears to be white makeup
on its face and all other exposed skin.

01:51:08.160 --> 01:51:13.020
Though these aspects of its appearance seem
as if they should be removable, the clothing

01:51:13.020 --> 01:51:19.380
and makeup are, in fact, parts of the entity's
physiology, and cannot be removed from its

01:51:19.380 --> 01:51:19.500
body.

01:51:19.500 --> 01:51:23.820
This is not the only unusual aspect of the
entity's physical form.

01:51:23.820 --> 01:51:30.000
Though it looks corporeal and solid, the entity
cannot touch or directly interact with any

01:51:30.000 --> 01:51:33.600
solid matter, with one particular exception.

01:51:33.600 --> 01:51:39.300
There is a colony of spiders living on and
inside of SCP-3247.

01:51:39.300 --> 01:51:48.780
These spiders have been officially designated
SCP-3247-A, and are highly protective of SCP-3247.

01:51:48.780 --> 01:51:55.260
If anyone or anything attempts to approach
SCP-3247 in a threatening manner, the spiders

01:51:55.260 --> 01:51:56.940
will swarm the potential threat.

01:51:56.940 --> 01:52:02.160
As any savvy anomalous activity enthusiast
might have already gathered, these are, of

01:52:02.160 --> 01:52:04.380
course, no ordinary spiders.

01:52:04.380 --> 01:52:10.800
Not only do they dwell on and in an intangible
mime, but they have a peculiar response to

01:52:10.800 --> 01:52:16.200
witnessing a human being making specific gestures
or pantomiming activities.

01:52:16.200 --> 01:52:21.000
When this occurs, the colony of spiders will
form the shape of an object related to the

01:52:21.000 --> 01:52:25.800
gestures, which they will then hold for up
to three hours, or until given additional

01:52:25.800 --> 01:52:28.440
stimuli that prompt a change in shape.

01:52:28.440 --> 01:52:32.820
While the spider colony is assembled into
a shape, they will be able to share some of

01:52:32.820 --> 01:52:35.580
the given objects' functions in spite of being&nbsp;

01:52:35.580 --> 01:52:38.160
technically nothing more than&nbsp;
a mass of well-coordinated

01:52:38.160 --> 01:52:39.240
arachnids.

01:52:39.240 --> 01:52:45.240
As for SCP-3247, it is either incapable of
speech or unwilling to speak.

01:52:45.240 --> 01:52:49.380
Instead, it communicates with Foundation staff
via silent miming.

01:52:49.380 --> 01:52:54.360
When it does, the spiders will frequently
react to its gestures, becoming, effectively,

01:52:54.360 --> 01:52:55.500
living props.

01:52:55.500 --> 01:53:02.220
SCP-3247 does not seem to be especially thrilled
with this, likely because miming is inherently

01:53:02.220 --> 01:53:07.500
a propless art form, and these spider-based
props undermine its artistic vision.

01:53:07.500 --> 01:53:12.840
Otherwise, though, the presence of the spiders
does not seem to bother SCP-3247.

01:53:12.840 --> 01:53:20.040
In order to better understand the nature of
SCP-3247-A, Foundation Staff conducted a series

01:53:20.040 --> 01:53:20.820
of tests.

01:53:20.820 --> 01:53:26.700
In each test, a D-Class was given a gesture
to perform in the presence of SCP-3247.

01:53:26.700 --> 01:53:30.900
Then, the research staff would record the
spider colony's response.

01:53:30.900 --> 01:53:36.600
During the first test, the research staff
ordered D-11424 to attempt to get as close

01:53:36.600 --> 01:53:39.180
to SCP-3247 as possible.

01:53:39.180 --> 01:53:42.060
They did not, of course, warn him about the
spiders.

01:53:42.060 --> 01:53:47.160
He entered the testing chamber and approached
the mime, who was pantomiming the act of climbing

01:53:47.160 --> 01:53:47.640
stairs.

01:53:47.640 --> 01:53:54.300
As the mime pretended to ascend an invisible
staircase, and D-11424 grew closer, instances

01:53:54.300 --> 01:54:01.260
of SCP-3247-A emerged to take on the shape
of a staircase, much to the mime's frustration.

01:54:01.260 --> 01:54:07.800
SCP-3247 stopped its performance, throwing
up its hands in a gesture of defeat.

01:54:07.800 --> 01:54:13.800
The spiders turned their attention to D-11424,
and began to swarm him, treating him as a

01:54:13.800 --> 01:54:14.520
potential threat.

01:54:14.520 --> 01:54:20.700
Panicking, and unsure how to communicate with
SCP-3247 while the spiders were overpowering

01:54:20.700 --> 01:54:24.540
him, D-11424 began to wave frantically at
the mime.

01:54:24.540 --> 01:54:28.860
The mime simply shrugged, giving him a look
that said "Well, what do you want me to do

01:54:28.860 --> 01:54:29.400
about it?"

01:54:29.400 --> 01:54:35.280
At this point, Control intervened, instructing
D-11424 to pantomime some kind of activity.

01:54:35.280 --> 01:54:41.580
Fortunately, before turning to a life of crime,
D-11424 had spent several years in a professional

01:54:41.580 --> 01:54:44.700
improv troupe, and was well-acquainted with
pantomime.

01:54:44.700 --> 01:54:48.300
His performing instincts kicked in, and he
leaped into action.

01:54:48.300 --> 01:54:52.080
He put a hand to his ear, as if listening
to the ringing of a telephone.

01:54:52.080 --> 01:54:56.040
The spiders stopped their attack, responding
immediately to his cue.

01:54:56.040 --> 01:55:01.020
They formed into the shape of a small table,
with an old-fashioned rotary phone on top.

01:55:01.020 --> 01:55:05.820
The mime rolled its eyes in disdain at the
sight of this prop-based performance, but

01:55:05.820 --> 01:55:07.800
D-11424 was on a roll.

01:55:07.800 --> 01:55:11.340
He crossed to the phone, picked up the receiver,
and held it to his ear.

01:55:11.340 --> 01:55:12.000
"Hello?"

01:55:12.000 --> 01:55:13.500
He asked, out of habit.

01:55:13.500 --> 01:55:16.140
He wasn't expecting to hear a voice on the
other line.

01:55:16.140 --> 01:55:17.820
But then, he did.

01:55:17.820 --> 01:55:23.220
Or rather, he heard the approximation of a
human voice, created by a swarm of anomalous

01:55:23.220 --> 01:55:23.700
spiders.

01:55:23.700 --> 01:55:29.160
It sounded a bit like a human voice sped up,
high-pitched and squeaky, speaking some sort

01:55:29.160 --> 01:55:29.880
of gibberish.

01:55:29.880 --> 01:55:35.880
Realizing that this was his moment to escape,
D-11424 placed the phone back in place, and

01:55:35.880 --> 01:55:37.620
promptly left the testing chamber.

01:55:37.620 --> 01:55:41.940
The spiders remained in the shape of the rotary
phone and the table for the next two hours,

01:55:41.940 --> 01:55:47.340
at which point they disassembled and returned
to their home on SCP-3247.

01:55:47.340 --> 01:55:53.100
After his surprisingly creative work in this
first test, it was decided that D-11424 would

01:55:53.100 --> 01:56:00.060
be the designated test subject for all future
testing with SCP-3247, provided that additional

01:56:00.060 --> 01:56:02.100
complications did not arise.

01:56:02.100 --> 01:56:08.520
Though he wasn't especially fond of spiders,
D-11424 was more than happy to accept the

01:56:08.520 --> 01:56:10.800
assignment, not that he had much choice in
the matter.

01:56:10.800 --> 01:56:16.800
Still, it was definitely a better deal than
getting fed to SCP-682, and it was a nice

01:56:16.800 --> 01:56:20.580
excuse to use his improv skills again after
a long retirement.

01:56:20.580 --> 01:56:26.700
During the second test, D-11424 knew what
to expect from SCP-3247.

01:56:26.700 --> 01:56:32.220
For this test, he was told to pantomime playing
tug of war with an invisible opponent and

01:56:32.220 --> 01:56:33.300
an invisible rope.

01:56:33.300 --> 01:56:38.220
Now that he knew his improvisational scene
partner would be a colony of spiders, he was

01:56:38.220 --> 01:56:40.380
able to enter the testing chamber with confidence.

01:56:40.380 --> 01:56:45.660
Once inside, he began to pantomime, pulling
on a rope, having that rope tugged away from

01:56:45.660 --> 01:56:48.780
him by a strong opponent, and struggling to
pull back.

01:56:48.780 --> 01:56:53.520
The spiders reacted right away, arranging
themselves into the shapes of a long rope,

01:56:53.520 --> 01:56:59.820
one side of which was in D-11424's hands,
as well as a large, humanoid, vaguely masculine

01:56:59.820 --> 01:57:01.980
shape that was holding the other side of the
rope.

01:57:01.980 --> 01:57:07.620
The spiders gave the rope a sharp tug, causing
D-11424 to lose his balance and fall over,

01:57:07.620 --> 01:57:09.540
the rope slipping out of his grasp.

01:57:09.540 --> 01:57:13.560
Aside from some injury to his pride, he was
otherwise unharmed.

01:57:13.560 --> 01:57:20.220
During Test 3, D-11424 was instructed to enter
the testing chamber and close his fist, while

01:57:20.220 --> 01:57:25.200
extending the thumb and index finger in the
gesture colloquially known as "finger guns."

01:57:25.200 --> 01:57:30.300
Sure enough, as soon as he assumed this position,
the spiders assembled into the shape of a

01:57:30.300 --> 01:57:30.660
handgun.

01:57:30.660 --> 01:57:35.820
D-11424 was then instructed to pick up the
spider gun and squeeze the place where the

01:57:35.820 --> 01:57:39.960
trigger would be if it were a real gun and
not, you know, spiders.

01:57:39.960 --> 01:57:45.000
A loud cracking sound was heard when the D-Class
squeezed, as a spider shot out of the barrel

01:57:45.000 --> 01:57:50.700
of the gun at high speed before smacking into
the nearby wall, leaving a small hole in the

01:57:50.700 --> 01:57:51.120
surface.

01:57:51.120 --> 01:57:57.300
D-11424 fired several more times, each shot
firing an individual spider at a pace that

01:57:57.300 --> 01:58:01.020
attending researchers described as "faster
than a speeding bullet."

01:58:01.020 --> 01:58:06.900
After firing six rounds of spiders at the
wall, D-11424 was instructed to place the

01:58:06.900 --> 01:58:08.280
spider gun back on the ground.

01:58:08.280 --> 01:58:14.940
During test 76, D-11424 was ordered to hold
his hands together and wiggle four fingers

01:58:14.940 --> 01:58:17.940
on each hand, effectively pantomiming a spider.

01:58:17.940 --> 01:58:22.500
The research team was curious to see what
the spiders would do when presented with a

01:58:22.500 --> 01:58:25.140
shape that matched their usual, unassembled
form.

01:58:25.140 --> 01:58:32.160
SCP-3247, who generally did not react much
to the experiments on its spiders, began shaking

01:58:32.160 --> 01:58:38.040
its head in mild disappointment as approximately
six hundred and forty spiders emerged from

01:58:38.040 --> 01:58:40.560
its body, dividing themselves into groups
of eight.

01:58:40.560 --> 01:58:46.260
Each group of eight spiders then joined forces
to form one larger spider, leaving eight spiders.

01:58:46.260 --> 01:58:51.840
These eight then split into pairs, who joined
together into one larger spider, and so on

01:58:51.840 --> 01:58:57.480
and so forth until there was one single giant
spider made from the hundreds of smaller spiders.

01:58:57.480 --> 01:59:03.480
At this point, D-11424 followed his heart,
jumping onto the mega-spider's back and riding

01:59:03.480 --> 01:59:08.460
it like a bull at the rodeo, as the spider
bucked and ran back and forth across the room.

01:59:08.460 --> 01:59:13.500
According to official transcripts, D-11424
yelled "yee-haw!"

01:59:13.500 --> 01:59:17.460
throughout this part of the test, until the
head researcher ordered him to climb down

01:59:17.460 --> 01:59:19.320
from the spider and exit the room.

01:59:19.320 --> 01:59:23.820
He was reprimanded for his behavior, and warned
that, if he acted without approval again,

01:59:23.820 --> 01:59:26.640
he would be taken off of&nbsp;
the project and reassigned&nbsp;

01:59:26.640 --> 01:59:29.220
to a much less enjoyable position as one of

01:59:29.220 --> 01:59:31.920
the designated eyes on SCP-173.

01:59:31.920 --> 01:59:36.660
D-11424 immediately agreed to comply with
future instructions.

01:59:36.660 --> 01:59:43.380
During Test 133, D-11424 was sent into the
testing chamber and told to shadowbox.

01:59:43.380 --> 01:59:48.000
He danced back and forth across the cell,
doing his best Sylvester Stallone impression

01:59:48.000 --> 01:59:50.880
and throwing punches in the general direction
of the spiders.

01:59:50.880 --> 01:59:58.320
In response, approximately 3000 spiders poured
out of SCP-3247, assembling into the shadowy

01:59:58.320 --> 02:00:01.860
shape of a boxer, and began to attack D-11424.

02:00:01.860 --> 02:00:07.920
The mass of spiders conducted itself at the
level of a professional boxer, dodging D-11424's

02:00:07.920 --> 02:00:13.500
hits before coming back at him with a jab,
cross, lead uppercut, and rear uppercut before

02:00:13.500 --> 02:00:14.580
he could defend himself.

02:00:14.580 --> 02:00:20.460
D-11424 fell to the ground, unconscious, and
guards were forced to interrupt the test in

02:00:20.460 --> 02:00:24.720
order to remove him from the room and take
him to the infirmary for medical treatment.

02:00:24.720 --> 02:00:32.940
After taking some time to recuperate, D-11424
returned to testing with SCP-3247-A. He was

02:00:32.940 --> 02:00:35.760
instructed to mime steering a wheel, such
as that of a car.

02:00:35.760 --> 02:00:41.880
Immediately, a number of spiders previously
unseen during testing emerged from SCP-3247,

02:00:41.880 --> 02:00:44.760
arranging themselves into the shape of a sedan.

02:00:44.760 --> 02:00:50.100
D-11424 was then commanded to climb inside
of the spider car and see if he could start

02:00:50.100 --> 02:00:50.280
it.

02:00:50.280 --> 02:00:54.360
He refused, insisting "I'm not getting in
a spider car, are you nuts?!"

02:00:54.360 --> 02:00:58.500
When pressed by Control to comply with orders,
he made a rude hand gesture.

02:01:00.000 --> 02:01:05.040
The spiders began to scramble to reassemble
themselves in response to the changed gesture,

02:01:05.040 --> 02:01:09.480
prompting Control to stop the test early to
spare the researchers' sensibilities.

02:01:09.480 --> 02:01:15.720
With strict guidelines to avoid inappropriate
or violent gestures, D-11424 was sent back

02:01:15.720 --> 02:01:20.520
into the testing chamber with instructions
to try out a variety of animal-inspired gestures

02:01:20.520 --> 02:01:21.780
in rapid succession.

02:01:21.780 --> 02:01:26.520
He formed one hand into a fist, and made a
peace sign with the other hand, putting them

02:01:26.520 --> 02:01:28.260
together to make a snail.

02:01:28.260 --> 02:01:33.120
As he made his hand snail crawl through the
air, the spiders crawled onto the floor and

02:01:33.120 --> 02:01:36.840
assembled into the shape of a snail in front
of D-11424.

02:01:36.840 --> 02:01:41.820
Though the spiders moved quickly, at their
usual scuttling pace, once they formed into

02:01:41.820 --> 02:01:44.640
the snail, they slowed to a gradual creep.

02:01:44.640 --> 02:01:51.120
D-11424 noted a shiny, slimy trail left behind
on the floor as the spider-snail moved.

02:01:51.120 --> 02:01:55.860
He was asked to consider touching it, but
refused, simply saying, "ew, no."

02:01:55.860 --> 02:01:59.880
Next, he took his hands and formed the shape
of a wolf's head, howling at the moon.

02:01:59.880 --> 02:02:04.680
The research staff were curious to see if
the spiders would form a wolf's head, or the

02:02:04.680 --> 02:02:05.820
animal's entire body.

02:02:05.820 --> 02:02:11.340
They got their answer as the spiders swarmed
and shifted, forming the shape of a full-sized

02:02:11.340 --> 02:02:12.000
grey wolf.

02:02:12.000 --> 02:02:16.920
The wolf padded back and forth across the
room, before sitting down, lifting its head,

02:02:16.920 --> 02:02:21.780
and emitting an audible howl that sounded
almost indistinguishable from the real thing.

02:02:21.780 --> 02:02:27.120
Next, D-11424 crossed his thumbs over each
other, fluttering his hands like a pair of

02:02:27.120 --> 02:02:27.360
wings.

02:02:27.360 --> 02:02:33.060
The spiders separated into smaller groups
and came together to form butterflies similar

02:02:33.060 --> 02:02:34.380
in size to a monarch.

02:02:34.380 --> 02:02:40.440
These spider butterflies began to flap their
wings, and, much to D-11424's surprise, they

02:02:40.440 --> 02:02:43.440
took flight and swirled through the air around
him.

02:02:43.440 --> 02:02:48.300
The D-Class was so moved by the beautiful
sight that he shed a single tear, which he

02:02:48.300 --> 02:02:50.040
promptly wiped away out of embarrassment.

02:02:50.040 --> 02:02:53.280
Control then prompted him to try the next
animal gesture.

02:02:53.280 --> 02:02:57.180
D-11424 used his hands to form the shape of
a rabbit.

02:02:57.180 --> 02:03:03.360
Several of the spiders crawled away, returning
to SCP-3247, and the remaining spiders took

02:03:03.360 --> 02:03:04.680
on the form of a rabbit.

02:03:04.680 --> 02:03:09.360
The spider-rabbit hopped realistically around
the room, twitching its ears and tail.

02:03:09.360 --> 02:03:14.160
At this point, D-11424 was instructed to offer
the spider rabbit a carrot.

02:03:14.160 --> 02:03:17.520
He produced a carrot from his pocket, holding
it out in front of him.

02:03:17.520 --> 02:03:22.680
The spider-rabbit hopped over to him, and,
one crunch at a time, began to eat the carrot

02:03:22.680 --> 02:03:24.060
until none remained.

02:03:24.060 --> 02:03:28.620
D-11424 appeared shaken up, and asked to leave
the testing chamber.

02:03:28.620 --> 02:03:32.340
As he had followed all of his instructions,
this request was granted.

02:03:32.340 --> 02:03:36.660
When he exited the chamber, all he would say
was "Where the hell did the carrot go?

02:03:36.660 --> 02:03:39.360
It doesn't have a stomach...it doesn't have
a mouth...where'd it go?"

02:03:39.360 --> 02:03:46.440
SCP-3247 is kept in an isolated chamber located
in the arachnid wing of Area-12.

02:03:46.440 --> 02:03:51.180
It does not appear to require food or rest,
but it has been provided with a television

02:03:51.180 --> 02:03:54.360
and a collection of silent films for morale
purposes.

02:03:54.360 --> 02:04:01.560
Instances of SCP-3247-A are fed via a fully
automated system that dispenses twenty grams

02:04:01.560 --> 02:04:03.180
of live crickets every week.

02:04:03.180 --> 02:04:08.340
Should a containment breach occur, staff have
been instructed to find a way to make escaped

02:04:08.340 --> 02:04:13.200
spiders take on a shape that renders them
motionless, then simply pick the spider cluster

02:04:13.200 --> 02:04:15.600
up and place it back inside of the cell.

02:04:15.600 --> 02:04:20.340
It is unlikely that the Foundation will ever
get an explanation for where the intangible

02:04:20.340 --> 02:04:24.240
mime, and his merry band of spider performers,
originated from.

02:04:24.240 --> 02:04:30.060
But one thing is clear, they won't be performing
in public again any time soon.

